SELECT r."title", r."content", r."duration", r."lesson_id", r."module_id", r."created_at", r."updated_at", r."description", r."order_index"
FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"Prove Rohit’s login is blocked","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Check disabled state and prove a new Rohit login cannot succeed.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 25\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe check_state.py independent-revoke\nRUN / PERFORM:\nPowerShell: run checker and fresh-login test.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nSTATE CHECK: PASS\nNew login as rohit.nair -> REJECTED\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nNEW private browser window: RohitLab!2026.\nAttempt fresh Report Portal sign-in.\nNo successful authenticated session allowed.\nRecord actual result, not the expected wording.\nUNDERSTAND:\nThe system must enforce the removal; a completed ticket alone is not enough.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 81–82 (Guided task 25). Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"40","lesson_id":"008345f3-56ab-4436-b6c9-fa40f4036dd5","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:14.778627+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:14.778627+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Open the forecast manager request","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Identify the boundary between closed actuals, forecast assumptions, budget plan and unapproved management actions.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"0083fcd0-36af-48e9-92c5-a082d6aa224a","module_id":"65f46751-f888-4cef-8899-82a916f8d88f","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:00.521491+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:00.521491+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Environmental Monitoring, Risk and Engineering Decisions","content":"Choose monitoring objectives and stations, and distinguish access readiness from actual sampling. Identify hazards, exposure and risk priorities. Compare engineering options against evidence, cost and authority limits. Separate planned costs, conditional approvals, commitments, payments and closure decisions.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"01c898c2-5e5d-4e5a-97fa-330be9d2d46f","module_id":"ee100c09-ed32-41bf-9d6e-7db5647fdf04","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:39.201442+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:39.201442+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Grade 9 Chemistry — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 9 Chemistry course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"029cd1e4-66a0-4eb7-a194-2d4ecafaa5eb","module_id":"c5d09bfe-cd27-415f-b6f8-e5d9e1aa3e6d","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:21.743329+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:21.743329+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Environmental Microbiology and Biodegradation","content":"Identify microorganisms and their role in water. Compare aerobic and anaerobic processes and see how biofilms form on surfaces. Learn the difference between culture counts and statistical indicator tests. Work through growth and microbial reporting examples.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"02e7b0a0-da97-4e62-8795-a508e1ab71ec","module_id":"3db5a5c9-e4bd-44f6-b0fd-20144804b713","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:29.259069+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:29.259069+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Explain the EBITDA shortfall","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Check the expected EBITDA gap of Rs 49,000, identify the evidence behind cost increases and prepare a non-approving manager interpretation.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"03005d00-82ce-488e-8d36-7e4bea97ad92","module_id":"5d6e6c3b-27f1-4069-9272-fb255d0feb98","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:56.559147+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:56.559147+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Receive the Week 4 final-results request","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 5 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Open Module 5 deck and workbook from the ZIP. Understand unique confirmed trials and why platform events must not be double counted.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"03873c2f-79ad-479b-9e98-c43789d2a9c2","module_id":"f555663a-aca5-4d75-b223-634f30c3762b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:47.713706+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:47.713706+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Create the candidate and document transfer records","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 09_Transfer_Tracker and 10_Transfer_Documents by candidate ID using only the new source evidence.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"70","lesson_id":"049daa98-33cb-4926-b860-ae2c078a7c26","module_id":"1a9397ae-439a-4b11-a6a7-a53ccaa97535","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:20.58804+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:20.58804+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Understand the September profit question","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Read why revenue above budget does not guarantee EBITDA above budget; locate the two related tasks in the guided deck.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"04fa43f7-2b98-4dc1-a13e-56fc648d0081","module_id":"5d6e6c3b-27f1-4069-9272-fb255d0feb98","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:54.294762+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:54.294762+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Environmental Data Analysis and Scientific Reasoning","content":"Match source records using sample IDs and identify missing or duplicate entries. Calculate averages and changes from dated readings. Read a time-series graph with missing values, then compare absolute and percentage change. Use a scatterplot to understand correlation without assuming causation.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"0524b1c0-52c4-46bd-8948-cb32716818bc","module_id":"a40751af-bf86-4569-afed-95138ce35e86","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:37.353468+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:37.353468+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Receive your first IAM support ticket","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Work as a junior IAM Operations Analyst at the fictional Cedar Retail service desk. The approved joiner request IAM-J-101 is for Ananya Shah (EMP-1042; username ananya.shah), requesting Finance Reports VIEW only.\nWORK REQUEST: Verify the employee identity and required approvals; create her account; grant viewer access; check the application; save proof.\nEXPECTED RESULT: Viewing the report succeeds (HTTP 200), editing is denied (HTTP 403), and the ticket has supporting evidence.\nCHECK: The account and permissions must match the request. Do not assume an urgent request is approved.\nUNDERSTAND: Your job is not to create every requested permission; it is to implement only verified, authorized access.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 1–2. Module 01 (Engage).","duration":"20","lesson_id":"05509af4-990a-4a15-b0eb-4a76664697fc","module_id":"e3fe24fa-601b-4db2-8e4a-d03421c93044","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:00.822875+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:00.822875+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Watch and learn: Asha investigates the advertisement","content":"Watch how Asha reads the offer and uses a sample study-app reading. Follow the working for Monday. Pause for the Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday calculations and record each step in your workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"05662334-48ab-48e5-89e1-9f9e61309f73","module_id":"fe9bc26e-1335-4f8c-a602-73bd583e43f5","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:51.737013+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:51.737013+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T26 - Give the campaign a clear name","content":"Work task T26: Give the campaign a clear name.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open the Campaign tab.\n2. Enter CA_L1_META_SALES_BLR_6D.\n3. Save campaign settings.\nCompleted example: Campaign name: CA_L1_META_SALES_BLR_6D.\nCheck in simulator: CA_L1_META_SALES_BLR_6D.\nWhy: Clear names help the team find the correct campaign.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (not yet uploaded to Drive): Module_05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign/M05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign.pptx\nLMS ADMIN ACTION: Upload this module deck separately before learner publication.","duration":"15","lesson_id":"06929001-61b5-4a72-a4c3-658b1d1a2c5f","module_id":"5e0d6e1b-e6fa-450d-93da-45fb48e4bcb7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:32.677673+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:32.677673+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"CA-002 Step 1 - Plan a new campaign","content":"Independent challenge CA-002: NEON NIGHT DUOS, a new fictional 2v2 PIXEL RUSH gaming event.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nStarting evidence: 4 paid teams, 8 open places, ₹2,400 maximum ad spend, ₹600 fee per duo. Event date: 30 November 2026.\nOpen: CA-002 in the same offline simulator. Work without copying the CLUTCH ARENA worked answers.\n1. Define the target\n2. Calculate the maximum cost per new duo\n3. Describe a suitable local adult audience\nCheck: submit the result in the simulator; correct mistakes using the source records.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nEvidence: save the new-case results and report actual outcomes even if the target is missed.\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1CSnOPP3lw9hO3pH_k7PoG00toEfdGWDv/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"45","lesson_id":"06af3b19-52a4-4a47-9258-9c260657fa94","module_id":"0a68386e-3c99-4b9d-807f-26b8f5103ed8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:46.90645+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:46.90645+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Read Day 60 manager and employee observations","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Inspect source notes for each employee, including issues that need supervised practice or manager resolution.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"06be046a-0598-4c51-ac6a-519d6cb39df7","module_id":"1d7fb1bb-786e-440a-8117-c59e29b8dda2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:14.344304+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:14.344304+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Evolve: Finance Analytics","content":"MODULE 1: Finance Analytics\n6E STAGE: Evolve\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nBUILD THE FINANCE POWER BI DASHBOARD\nLoad Fin_Performance and Fin_Working_Capital.\nLink Month and Region dimensions.\nCreate measures and 5 KPI cards: Revenue, Rev Var %, Operating Profit, Operating Margin %, CCC.\nAdd Budget vs Actual, Margin by Region and CCC visuals.\nAdd Month and Region slicers.\n\nRESOURCE: M1_Finance_Evolve.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M1_Evolve_Finance_Decision_Recommendation_Brief.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M1_Evolve_Finance_Decision_Recommendation_Brief.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1qB45BdEYMVFGUDvjosKROFyu6cBZQrFT/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"071537e9-d51c-4e52-9fcf-d340d967de9a","module_id":"a4e8da2a-aba5-4f08-b27c-c417f244968c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:17.795848+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:17.795848+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Reconcile Day 7 status across trackers","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Match Day 7 results, open issue owner and 02_Onboarding_Tracker; verify any required escalation or follow-up date.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"0777f9c4-b0a0-4b85-be3e-8b08943503d4","module_id":"fd462bb9-9a77-4355-ac64-2859a808c0f2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:10.378896+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:10.378896+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Open the simulator and find the five controls","content":"Download START_HERE.html from Drive, then open the saved HTML in Chrome or Edge. Find Temperature (C), Valid reading, WRITE TEMP, WRITE FLAGS, COMMIT and CHECK MY RESULT. It is a software model of Motor M-02, not live hardware. OUTPUT: simulator open with each field located.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"08895719-86dd-4f6b-9017-4e2ddb4c284b","module_id":"e05a5029-3776-445a-bdf7-209387c8eb3c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:23.849324+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:23.849324+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Delivery & Customer Evidence - Guided Learning and Practice","content":"Work through Tasks 36-42 with the module learning deck and operating workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"092a80a0-3ce1-4065-a8e0-90ae2d3360bc","module_id":"d75b16e7-d777-4243-8d9f-c1eab1517e64","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:41.55653+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:41.55653+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Clean and verify the analysis base","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: In M1_WORKING_DATA and M1_ANALYSIS, identify duplicate WS-2023, recoverable missing stores and non-delivered cases before calculating usable orders.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"65","lesson_id":"0954068b-fda2-4712-95c5-dffaca3eaa80","module_id":"9184ac19-93a3-42ea-90f1-0de8006dab18","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:12.181247+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:12.181247+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Choose two new tests and export nine results","content":"Finish all seven guided controller cases. Then choose your own meaningful HOT reading and a CLEAR reading, explain the rule briefly and check the result. Only after nine completed cases, choose Download my software evidence (CSV). The written explanation stays pending reviewer acceptance. OUTPUT: nine-case software-model CSV.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"0a3a1973-4673-4a3d-8a50-3aebda43c4b1","module_id":"68737413-f85b-4ebe-b5e4-4e4e1e5ad92b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:26.406374+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:26.406374+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Disable Ananya’s account","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Stop new authentication for the approved leaver.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 22\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, ROOT\ns = connect(\"IAM-L-301\")\nu = find_user(s, \"ananya.shah\")\nassert u, \"STOP: wrong identity\"\nr = s.put(f\"{ROOT}/users/{u[''id'']}\",\n          json={**u, \"enabled\": False}, timeout=15)\nr.raise_for_status()\nprint(\"ENABLED:\", find_user(s, \"ananya.shah\")[\"enabled\"])\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nENABLED: False\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nKeycloak Enabled must now be OFF.\nFinance-Viewers must remain absent.\nDo not assume an old browser session has ended.\nUNDERSTAND:\nDisabling login and removing entitlements are separate operations.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 75–76 (Guided task 22). Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"35","lesson_id":"0c524360-de99-4928-95ed-38130c24d306","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:13.927045+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:13.927045+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Correct the T04 failure and perform retest","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Use the given corrected observation to complete T04-R and M5_VALIDATION!B27 pilot readiness; explain remaining risks.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"0cb4fef9-071b-4a30-988e-0614170bd6f2","module_id":"3df6a56d-ec9f-466e-a689-aa94bd08320a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:24.171901+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:24.171901+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S42 - Containerize the same Grama app","content":"WHAT: We are packaging Grama’s existing client and server for repeatable execution.\nDO: Build and run the SAME Grama app with Docker Compose. Create a NEW pending record in the Docker volume, restart container and verify its ID.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: A new SUG-ID survives a Docker restart in the container database.\nIF IT FAILS: Stop the old Node server to free port 3000; the earlier local SQLite file does not automatically transfer.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 07 PowerPoint, task S42 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S42.","duration":"90","lesson_id":"0d4d4fba-1a1d-42bb-b0eb-c4a762bfb32d","module_id":"f2a32bfe-3e30-4928-ab08-81ec0f90db87","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:57.971453+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:57.971453+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Module 01 - The Lunch Mystery and Food Routes","content":"Follow the approved BODY QUEST slides 1-13 (13 slides). Pause to attempt every question in writing before checking the answer, use feedback, and retry where requested.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"0d6eadce-d6b3-48f8-b35e-ee37732bb44c","module_id":"aa2cbdb6-2576-4e8c-bd47-35424cd48948","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:56.423866+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:56.423866+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Read a FAIL, correct it and save the test evidence","content":"Compare expected and actual T04 behaviour, inspect the assigned code, fix the faulty comparison and rerun all required tests. A valid software PASS needs the unchanged 14-case suite and generated learner_c.log, learner_bus_trace.csv and learner_c_status.json. Missing or changed proof invalidates acceptance. OUTPUT: reviewable M-02 software evidence.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"0df9acba-d5f4-416a-9d91-a0b0de19a4ed","module_id":"384d0feb-b2bd-4611-a17a-dba0f96c9ada","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:28.964318+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:28.964318+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Verify pilot formulas and metrics","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: In M6_PILOT inspect pilot affected-rate and weighted confirmation-time formulas; compare the 30.0 percent baseline with 6.6 percent pilot.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"0e1198ad-8d1b-4633-88d2-98011d6d0ab3","module_id":"144a0889-2ac7-47f6-8cea-a450a7efd3f1","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:26.727258+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:26.727258+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Read an existing real account","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Watch the reference runner execute the displayed code in the isolated reference realm. You will type the exact code on the next I TRY slide.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 03\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, group_names\ns = connect()\nu = find_user(s, \"demo.viewer\")\nassert u, \"Missing baseline user\"\nprint(\"USER:\", u[\"username\"])\nprint(\"ENABLED:\", u[\"enabled\"])\nprint(\"GROUPS:\", group_names(s, u[\"id\"]))\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nUSER: demo.viewer\nENABLED: True\nGROUPS: [''Finance-Viewers'']\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nThe account exists exactly once.\nFinance-Viewers is its only group.\nAlso run in PowerShell:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe check_state.py baseline\nUNDERSTAND:\nA user account and its group assignments are different pieces of evidence.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 24–25 (Guided task 03). Module 02 (Explore).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"0f2fa60e-6ee7-4270-9ac5-af707f65f10f","module_id":"11649aa6-8081-45b1-bd24-94c42727b4dd","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:04.51493+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:04.51493+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Run the independent onboarding quality check","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Check all seven transfer sheets, identify unresolved evidence, and hand off the new-case portfolio without copying the main-case answers.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"100638c7-628b-4a3e-a985-83afcb9b4f1e","module_id":"1a9397ae-439a-4b11-a6a7-a53ccaa97535","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:22.856486+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:22.856486+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"Opportunity & Feasibility - Guided Learning and Practice","content":"Work through Tasks 01-05 with the module learning deck and operating workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"102200fc-0ce7-418f-98a6-8fb6d76ad99b","module_id":"75e85e2d-2718-4140-9dfc-a16e82cec118","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:32.813744+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:32.813744+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Write the customer positioning and measurable objective","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 2 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Complete workbook 02_Direction using the highest-supported pattern, customer need, verified product proof and a time-bounded result.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"105cfbf7-0dac-486d-a5d5-1d8d9a5ff25d","module_id":"82d21194-c6d2-4f91-8a31-17f8e16bde2d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:38.332289+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:38.332289+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S11 - Filter resources by village","content":"WHAT: We are adding a village dropdown that shows only local resource cards.\nDO: Add the village dropdown inside the styled .filters area and extend the filtering logic in app.js.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: With other filters cleared, selecting Melur shows GRC-002 and GRC-007.\nIF IT FAILS: Reset search and category to avoid a hidden old filter.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 02 PowerPoint, task S11 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S11.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"10c90aac-c694-4a6e-a985-7d46473e192a","module_id":"7a584fec-8468-485f-aad3-a5fe02e103ca","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:38.900545+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:38.900545+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"Inspect the baseline and pilot observations","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read the source without collapsing exception types into one average; check which metrics have acceptance boundaries.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"10c9a801-6717-488f-bec3-9cf7839ae8fc","module_id":"144a0889-2ac7-47f6-8cea-a450a7efd3f1","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:26.163206+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:26.163206+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Submit guided IAM evidence for human review","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Deliver a completed guided ticket lifecycle to the simulated IAM supervisor.\nPRECONDITIONS: Save the approved tickets, IAM state snapshots, actual portal 200/403 events, separate leaver evidence and HOLD decision. Keep earlier joiner proof intact.\nRUN:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe handover.py guided\nCHECK: Open handover/outbox/IAM_L1_queue_submission.json. Confirm Queue: IAM-REVIEW and Status: pending human acceptance.\nRESULT: A queue receipt for the guided evidence packet; receipt is not a certification.\nUNDERSTAND: A saved file or a printed PASS does not prove that the required reviewer received acceptable evidence.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 87. Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"25","lesson_id":"1149636e-f71d-487d-b4b4-3e684710b4d1","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.635943+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.635943+00:00","description":null,"order_index":9},{"title":"S31 - Connect search to API query filters","content":"WHAT: We are sending search, village and category to SQLite through the API.\nDO: Send search text, village and category as query parameters to the API; reset all three controls before each known-answer test.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Combined filters match the expected verified resources without leftover filter values.\nIF IT FAILS: Clear stale selected filters and inspect the request URL.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 05 PowerPoint, task S31 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S31.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"12936ed1-16b9-4963-a01a-e73ca93aee02","module_id":"cb186bda-f107-4d57-bf65-07aa218b21ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:51.149756+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:51.149756+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Record Day 7 employee and manager check-ins","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 06_Followup_Checkins for the Day 7 checkpoint with employee update, manager update and HR result.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"129f5fdc-927e-474b-ba8f-cbbe544a2ae2","module_id":"fd462bb9-9a77-4355-ac64-2859a808c0f2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:09.247494+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:09.247494+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3}]'::jsonb) r
