FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"Inspect the September invoice evidence","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: In the untouched Source Data file, read SEP_SALES product, pack and net-sales columns; check periods, identifiers and any exception evidence before calculation.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"149bd243-e817-40ed-af2c-3b6973beeb65","module_id":"256300bc-d9a5-4ac7-b553-8db9932a5b71","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:51.739727+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:51.739727+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"T02 - Remove invalid records","content":"Work task T02: Remove invalid records.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Team bookings in the shared offline simulator.\n1. In Team bookings, tick Exclude invalid records.\n2. Look at the duplicate and test rows.\n3. Type the clean starting total.\nCompleted example: Exclude: Tests, duplicates, failed and cancelled; Correct starting total: 5.\nCheck in simulator: 5.\nWhy: Bad rows must not use tournament places.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1qf78k8RvV7GgG3Rm725jIXzCtZ4LDmes/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"15b0f0c8-4784-4209-bf8e-6d634c5813ef","module_id":"681f39c1-fc77-4026-b85b-29f1521668ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:17.910894+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:17.910894+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Submit the seven-module BA portfolio","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Use the guided final checklist to confirm each module output is complete, navigable and ready for Operations Manager review.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"15e70013-e4f7-4a7b-a1a1-03df87deb30e","module_id":"61953943-322d-4034-ad05-89c9b5a237af","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:30.969753+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:30.969753+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Engage: Final Submission and Oral Defence","content":"MODULE 5: Final Submission and Oral Defence\n6E STAGE: Engage\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nFINAL SUBMISSION SUMMARY\nProblem\n5 Findings\n3 Actions\nLimitation\n\nRESOURCE: M5_Final_Submission_Engage.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"16772b7a-9b96-4dd7-848d-ae08f7bacb05","module_id":"b7fb8dde-5329-4c61-8197-4f52cdf3ccac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:29.309068+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:29.309068+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Explain the information gap and verify","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete the failure point and explanation in M2_AS_IS_MAP!F16:H23; separate observed process behavior from hypotheses.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"16991e13-1668-418a-9981-884e22f5f5a1","module_id":"00a3db8f-40b2-4d86-9c83-62c4bcc12ef3","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:16.449921+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:16.449921+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Receive the September revenue task","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder. COURSE SOURCE FOLDER: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12GS-I4h4a8j0NNDB8DgF8CdgWQf92X9U.\nDO: Read the Finance Manager request, identify SEP_SALES, SEP_EXCEPTIONS and SEP_GL_REVENUE, and understand that a raw invoice register is not necessarily posted ledger revenue.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"183a7fbc-3408-448b-a9ac-61b3ea982f74","module_id":"256300bc-d9a5-4ac7-b553-8db9932a5b71","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:51.173271+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:51.173271+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Test what the viewer can do","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Sign in as the existing viewer and test one allowed action and one denied action.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 04\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nStart-Process \"http://127.0.0.1:5000\"\nRUN / PERFORM:\nPowerShell: open portal. In private browser, test both actions.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nSIGNED IN: demo.viewer\nView report -> 200 | Report visible\nEdit report -> 403 | Access denied\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nUse a NEW private browser window on reference portal :5001.\nLog in as demo.viewer / DemoViewer!2026.\nClick View report, then Edit report.\nDo not pass without both observed results.\nUNDERSTAND:\nLogin answers WHO you are. Authorization answers WHAT you can do.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 26–27 (Guided task 04). Module 02 (Explore).","duration":"35","lesson_id":"19244911-308f-4607-8d6e-d092c11f85f3","module_id":"11649aa6-8081-45b1-bd24-94c42727b4dd","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:04.811656+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:04.811656+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Explain: HR Analytics","content":"MODULE 3: HR Analytics\n6E STAGE: Explain\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nHR — ANSWER CHECK\nSouth\nSouth shows higher workforce pressure and weaker recruitment conversion in Jul–Sep.\n\nRESOURCE: M3_HR_Explain.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"196256a5-e14d-4ccd-be67-e33f550c01ee","module_id":"8759a2fe-d783-4917-9716-d5383a2387ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:23.528283+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:23.528283+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Inspect October ledger and action records","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read OCT_SALES_CONTROL, OCT_ACTUALS and OCT_ACTION_RESULTS; identify the status and period of every source before deciding.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"1990cff9-b5ed-44ca-bcf2-edf8b49275c3","module_id":"056822e1-887b-4a10-99e9-70f234cd58b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:04.789627+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:04.789627+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Pre-Counseling: Session Introduction","content":"SESSION: Pre-Counseling\nINTRODUCTION: Participant introduction session. Start with a clear picture of your interests, strengths and goals. Session focus: Understand your starting point and identify a useful next step.\n\nSESSION PARTICIPATION STEPS\n1. Prepare: Keep your education background, interests and questions ready.\n2. Share: Describe what you enjoy, what feels difficult and what you hope to explore.\n3. Explore: Listen to possible pathways and ask questions before making decisions.\n4. Capture: Record the suggestions, unanswered questions and agreed next steps.\n\nSESSION FOCUS: Understand your starting point and identify a useful next step.\nRESOURCE: See linked presentation (Pre_Counseling_Introduction.pptx).","duration":"60","lesson_id":"19b2886c-d684-4e67-9447-4a620c2bb623","module_id":"54610cb4-d03e-45cc-9025-18417ffee6ba","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:43:00.040612+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:43:00.040612+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Calculate P&L budget variances","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 02_PNL using source-backed budget and actual amounts. Calculate sales, COGS, operating expense and EBITDA variances, checking the sign of expense overruns.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"19e63613-08fe-4ee1-8e5e-058963258f95","module_id":"5d6e6c3b-27f1-4069-9272-fb255d0feb98","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:55.427136+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:55.427136+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Update the main tracker and validate","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Cross-check 02_Onboarding_Tracker and 03_Document_Check with Day 1 evidence; do not mark an unresolved request ready.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"19e63739-c1e4-4974-9d7c-0b824fd9dcda","module_id":"022301cb-819a-4972-beb0-ed07f30a1312","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:07.248981+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:07.248981+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Find the assigned C file and read the decision","content":"Open assessment/assigned_firmware_host_demo.c in the extracted practice folder. Use Ctrl+F for TODO. Read sample_dc as temperature x10, <= as less than or equal to and >= as greater than or equal to. For an already-ON warning, sample_dc <= 650 means clear at 65C or below. OUTPUT: identify the two lines to change.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"1a8b06bc-dcd4-4f15-9a0d-0de8d1ac2f9a","module_id":"384d0feb-b2bd-4611-a17a-dba0f96c9ada","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:27.262794+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:27.262794+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Compare affected orders across branches","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Use prepared helper fields to compare branch delivered-order counts and affected rates; write store-level observations in M1_ANALYSIS!E16:E18.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"1b6280f5-0620-4602-875d-716fd705ba69","module_id":"9184ac19-93a3-42ea-90f1-0de8006dab18","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:12.746362+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:12.746362+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Grade 12 Physics — Energy, flow and sustainable water infrastructure","content":"Complete Grade 12 Physics course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"1b7af6a8-94db-4f31-9c10-f36cd3e8ef4f","module_id":"5f77e90d-a099-47ae-b251-49e5eeb17e7d","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:18:57.864662+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:18:57.864662+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Watch: The Coach Groups Coins (optional presentation)","content":"Watch the coach select coins and mark a full repeating unit. See how six groups reach coin 18. Make your own prediction about coin 20 before the worked answer appears.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"1b85ca34-1ea2-444b-bf71-50fb53f0a98e","module_id":"ac20b2cd-e39d-4173-a04f-67da9ce619c8","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:43.949062+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:43.949062+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Inspect channel reports and order exports","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read SwaadFit_M4_Source.xlsx, including Week 2 platform, orders and retail sampling observations; preserve date and event definitions.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"1b872bf2-4ba0-47a2-a835-58aa2a1234c2","module_id":"2563fa98-58f6-4862-80d8-934090fe4bad","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:44.576539+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:44.576539+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"S37 - Review and approve pending resources","content":"WHAT: We are giving only signed-in coordinators the ability to approve or reject suggestions.\nDO: Load full six-field pending records; inspect the two supplied fictional source notices before approving, rejecting or HOLDing. Preserve pending status on HOLD and show network-failure recovery.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Matching evidence may support a decision; conflicting/absent evidence is held or escalated. Failure does not falsely show Saved; retry only after reloading pending state.\nIF IT FAILS: Record source comparison in S37_SOURCE_REVIEW; verify actual notice content, not only a nonempty source string.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 06 PowerPoint, task S37 (original V25 teaching content).\nSOURCE DOCUMENTS: NOTICE-RR-026.png: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ofvZRT86QtcIBK6AKydQV4iN7fMR9lZ8/view?usp=drivesdk\nNOTICE-LIB-026.png: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uyFsKDKh8sDQV171vIVAb1hpf8IlV37Y/view?usp=drivesdk\nTEST SUBMISSIONS CSV: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gVYa0VJu0gCfhf6EjbQtU4rOhtW3wJbC/view?usp=drivesdk\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S37.","duration":"90","lesson_id":"1bdf5772-eee4-413e-ae0d-1910d7dcf27f","module_id":"700759e6-a8d5-4d9f-9c79-6e724f3c101a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:54.838945+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:54.838945+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"CA-002 Step 2 - Create new advertising assets","content":"Independent challenge CA-002: NEON NIGHT DUOS, a new fictional 2v2 PIXEL RUSH gaming event.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nStarting evidence: 4 paid teams, 8 open places, ₹2,400 maximum ad spend, ₹600 fee per duo. Event date: 30 November 2026.\nOpen: CA-002 in the same offline simulator. Work without copying the CLUTCH ARENA worked answers.\n1. Write two ads with approved facts\n2. Check both ads for false promises\n3. Export four readable PNG images\nCheck: submit the result in the simulator; correct mistakes using the source records.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nEvidence: save the new-case results and report actual outcomes even if the target is missed.\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1CSnOPP3lw9hO3pH_k7PoG00toEfdGWDv/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"50","lesson_id":"1ca5ea2c-5011-4ad3-ba2c-0bad54526053","module_id":"0a68386e-3c99-4b9d-807f-26b8f5103ed8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:47.473902+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:47.473902+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Environmental Chemistry and Pollutant Transformations","content":"Explain oxidation and reduction using electron transfer. Learn when dissolved substances may form a solid, how adsorption differs from absorption, and why pH changes chemical forms. Use solubility, adsorption and speciation calculations, then explain their limits.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"1e06ece0-a5c3-46cf-bf9e-0370959503b0","module_id":"bdf451d0-2465-4cf4-938b-91141822791c","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:27.867456+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:27.867456+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"S39 - Test protected Express HTTP requests","content":"WHAT: Test login and actual authorization, not just SQLite helpers.\nDO: Create and run protected Express HTTP tests for login, authorization, approval and rejection using test data.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Authorized decisions produce expected HTTP/data changes; unauthorized requests are blocked.\nIF IT FAILS: If Express is unavailable, mark BLOCKED—not PASS.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 07 PowerPoint, task S39 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S39.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"1ea42a3c-2e19-4d54-bf61-6d822ef2ef34","module_id":"f2a32bfe-3e30-4928-ab08-81ec0f90db87","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:56.263554+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:56.263554+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Finance & Controls - Guided Learning and Practice","content":"Work through Tasks 14-19 with the module learning deck and operating workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"1f12dee8-ee80-41d6-aa6f-47e0a7e175ca","module_id":"13e33f2e-f5d1-4be3-b136-16eb6ffbf5b8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:36.921929+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:36.921929+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Engage: Finance Analytics","content":"MODULE 1: Finance Analytics\n6E STAGE: Engage\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nFINANCE\nFINANCE TASK\nWhere is profitability and working-capital pressure concentrated?\nUse these sheets\n01_Fin_Performance\n02_Fin_Statements\n03_Fin_Working_Capital\nCalculate the required KPIs\nRevenue Variance, Revenue Variance %, Operating Profit, Operating Margin %, DSO, Inventory Days, DPO and Cash Conversion Cycle.\n\nRESOURCE: M1_Finance_Engage.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"1fab9bae-7208-4fa3-9061-ad826f2f19a5","module_id":"a4e8da2a-aba5-4f08-b27c-c417f244968c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:15.662385+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:15.662385+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Grade 10 English — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 10 English course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"22348063-a5aa-4328-a381-f1a8188c9d00","module_id":"674af85f-7871-47bd-833d-33f08acbf38f","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:39.813735+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:39.813735+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Start the new-company independent mission","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; GrainGlow files are inside 04_Independent_Practice. Use this ZIP source to avoid mixing versions. Read 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the work.\nDO: Open 04_Independent_Practice/GrainGlow_Early_Cycle_Independent_Challenge.pptx, GrainGlow_Transfer_Source.xlsx and GrainGlow_Transfer_Learner_Workbook.xlsx INSIDE the same integrated ZIP.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"2690d18d-adbb-4983-9478-e48edeb0b81b","module_id":"a97147bf-68b1-495a-b6d6-a3553e62ad46","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:51.99253+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:51.99253+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Receive the Motor M-03 engineering change","content":"New assigned motor: M-03. The training work order changes thresholds to 72C ON and 66C OFF, with invalid sensor readings still treated as FAULT. The M-02 result is your example, not the new answer. OUTPUT: write the two new threshold rules in words before editing.","duration":"25","lesson_id":"2723a969-22e1-46fb-91ff-c1f6ebdb4136","module_id":"d09eb39f-3151-4b13-a818-a75a632157f2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:29.817106+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:29.817106+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Evaluate improvement and cash-release actions","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 05_ACTION. Keep EBITDA options and cash-release proposals separate and mark all modeled benefits as subject to management approval.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"65","lesson_id":"278d1e92-38cb-4412-b55a-b26fc58f8e41","module_id":"65f46751-f888-4cef-8899-82a916f8d88f","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:02.805902+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:02.805902+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Explain the change and hand over the evidence","content":"State which two rules you changed, what the 11-case results prove and any issue needing review. Submit M-02 and M-03 software logs/source identifiers. A software-model or hosted-C PASS is not physical FPGA, motor, UART or 200 ms measurement acceptance; written explanation requires review. OUTPUT: review-ready introductory software handover.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"28804731-3f4c-4efc-9da9-654d6750f27f","module_id":"d09eb39f-3151-4b13-a818-a75a632157f2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:31.517718+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:31.517718+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Check findings, wording and authority","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Verify each statement has source, interpretation and an authorized next step; rewrite any overstated conclusions.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"28cd6d47-c94b-4565-9c9b-c5038f52a491","module_id":"61953943-322d-4034-ad05-89c9b5a237af","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:30.404852+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:30.404852+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Turn Student Interests into Learning — The Fractions Building Challenge","content":"Follow Ananya’s classroom story. Recognise the student interest, connect it to the fractions learning objective, observe AI-assisted preparation and the playable building challenge, and use feedback, retries and learning evidence to verify understanding.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"2a5a431f-29ba-4c33-a0d5-9f75827a633e","module_id":"8f497e3f-31c0-48ec-9807-e326fd4d502a","created_at":"2026-11-10T09:54:39.105729+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-10T09:54:39.105729+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T16 - Write two ads using only approved facts","content":"Work task T16: Write two ads using only approved facts.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ad creative studio in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Creative studio and read the approved organiser brief.\n2. Enter both ads using NOVA STRIKE, 5v5, Bengaluru, 27 October 2026, 18+ and ₹750/team.\n3. Check claims. Any contradictory age, fee, date or prize must be removed.\nCompleted example: Event: CLUTCH ARENA / NOVA STRIKE; Location: Bengaluru; Event date: 27 October 2026; Fee: ₹750/team; Age: 18+; Wrong prizes, dates, age claims: REJECTED.\nCheck in simulator: REJECTED.\nWhy: A good ad is truthful. Wrong fees, dates or age rules must fail.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1H-5eW5OhpLbO7DsFnlyXWDHHny8-3LO1/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"35","lesson_id":"2ad05a4a-df90-4c09-b30f-92e3da8d173b","module_id":"f2f23969-4104-4df2-a4a8-d8687fad4dc6","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:26.422882+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:26.422882+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S18 - Cache the offline frontend","content":"WHAT: We are enabling offline re-visits to static Grama files after an online visit.\nDO: Add network-first static-file caching in sw.js. Test online then offline, while excluding API/session data and preserving local drafts.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Static Grama pages can be revisited offline after being cached; local drafts are unchanged and protected API responses are not cached.\nIF IT FAILS: Clear ONLY Grama cache entries; do not clear all site data or erase localStorage.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 03 PowerPoint, task S18 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S18.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"2b09b6db-8972-4af2-adea-60a068c5eb8a","module_id":"725cf25c-1179-43c1-92b8-a16610df08b7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:43.171213+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:43.171213+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"S33 - Inspect pending database records","content":"WHAT: We are checking that submitted suggestions are stored as pending.\nDO: Create and run a script to inspect pending suggestions directly in SQLite.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The newly submitted SUG-ID is present with status pending.\nIF IT FAILS: Check the database location and exact ID, not just a total count.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 05 PowerPoint, task S33 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S33.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"2b1aa904-6145-4f51-b330-98e81827ade9","module_id":"cb186bda-f107-4d57-bf65-07aa218b21ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:52.289063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:52.289063+00:00","description":null,"order_index":8}]'::jsonb) r
