SELECT r."title", r."content", r."duration", r."lesson_id", r."module_id", r."created_at", r."updated_at", r."description", r."order_index"
FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"Shape Signal: Count Straight Sides","content":"Look at the drawn triangle, square and pentagon. Predict the next polygon. Count and mark edges during guided and independent work, then identify the rule that controls the side counts.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"2bad2e7a-43da-466b-9651-53519b0f2f05","module_id":"7c78ebee-8cbe-4c88-9b17-7dcdd312ccc4","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:48.130528+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:48.130528+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Record competitor evidence and stock availability","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 1 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Use the source store audits and Week 7 stock record. Complete the competitor observations and available-days calculations in the learner workbook.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"2bfd8016-e777-4605-a8b6-b1af5ab8229f","module_id":"29687f58-184a-4af4-a628-043d14f5d175","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:34.65074+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:34.65074+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Engage: Business Analytics","content":"MODULE 2: Business Analytics\n6E STAGE: Engage\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nBUSINESS ANALYTICS\nBUSINESS ANALYTICS TASK\nWhere is customer / fulfilment performance deteriorating and which process stages are bottlenecks?\nUse these sheets\n04_BA_Order_Data\n05_BA_Business_Context\n06_BA_Stakeholder_Inputs\n07_BA_Process_Data\nCalculate customer outcomes\nOrders, Average Order Value, Average Delivery Days, Return Rate, Complaint Rate and Satisfaction.\nCalculate process performance\nActual Stage Hours and Delay Hours.\n\nRESOURCE: M2_Business_Analytics_Engage.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"2c0358d7-a925-4f8c-b2da-8da09a5e1d18","module_id":"56bcb15d-8908-460a-9eb0-e8fe9461a59c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:19.104646+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:19.104646+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Examine option and process evidence","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Inspect the constraints behind Options A, B and C in the source pack without assuming authority to deploy any option.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"2c0de9af-2e14-45e8-bc61-3e6d0a240367","module_id":"4ebcf693-3bd3-4361-805c-aab771f99ee8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:20.420821+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:20.420821+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Check before creating Ananya","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Ticket IAM-J-101 is approved. First make sure ananya.shah does not already exist.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 05\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user\ns = connect()\nu = find_user(s, \"ananya.shah\")\nassert u is None, \"HOLD: username already exists\"\nprint(\"CHECK: username free; approved creation may start\")\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nCHECK: username free;\napproved creation may start\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nTicket IAM-J-101: APPROVED\nName Ananya Shah | EMP-1042\nananya.shah@example.test\nGroup Finance-Viewers; NOT Editors.\nUNDERSTAND:\nA duplicate identity is a stop condition, not a reason to invent another username.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 30–31 (Guided task 05). Module 03 (Explain).","duration":"40","lesson_id":"2c2fa087-66f7-4e3f-ba07-b3ab8971cf6d","module_id":"fc3b345d-ea20-4ef5-8693-9796ed1939b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:05.941207+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:05.941207+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Perform the evidence and approval review","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 5 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Use 07_Reason_Review to justify a chosen and rejected action. Check the worked handover only after completing the learner file.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"2c84f1c5-ea21-4baa-994b-0b309c17007c","module_id":"f555663a-aca5-4d75-b223-634f30c3762b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:51.142533+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:51.142533+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"T10 - Spot the repeated payment notice","content":"Work task T10: Spot the repeated payment notice.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Website & test checkout in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Safety tests and select your captured payment.\n2. Press Repeat payment notice. Check that the paid booking count did not rise.\n3. Later, in Tracking lab, reject the duplicate Purchase event.\nCompleted example: One captured payment: TX for CA-TEST-001; Repeat notice: Two messages, one booking; Tracking issue: Duplicate Purchase must be excluded.\nCheck in simulator: Duplicate Purchase must be excluded.\nWhy: A payment notice may arrive twice. Count the payment once only.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1tJuOwfbw-QCews6r6YS7DyDeJSIcPkOy/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"2d22b648-30bb-4b26-8cd4-6b16fde272bb","module_id":"5ed0a17f-83ab-4746-b1d6-8ab738d6f9eb","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:22.733873+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:22.733873+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Open the Week 2 execution assignment","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 4 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Open the Module 4 deck and workbook in the ZIP; identify execution status, channel KPIs and the difference between platform events and confirmed orders.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"2d74c303-0d38-493e-af68-a1cb6e6ae1d2","module_id":"2563fa98-58f6-4862-80d8-934090fe4bad","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:44.009272+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:44.009272+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T03 - Find the empty team slots","content":"Work task T03: Find the empty team slots.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Team bookings in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Look at the 16 team boxes in Bookings.\n2. Count the empty boxes.\n3. Enter the answer.\nCompleted example: Maximum teams: 16; Already booked: 5; Empty places: 11.\nCheck in simulator: 11.\nWhy: Empty places are the number of teams we still need.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1qf78k8RvV7GgG3Rm725jIXzCtZ4LDmes/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"15","lesson_id":"2de7caac-c525-4d01-805d-583de069cc08","module_id":"681f39c1-fc77-4026-b85b-29f1521668ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:18.478409+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:18.478409+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T39 - Count the new paid teams after Day 2","content":"Work task T39: Count the new paid teams after Day 2.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Team bookings in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Team bookings > All forms.\n2. Filter to Day 1 and Day 2, and Paid only.\n3. Enter the number of confirmed new paid teams.\nCompleted example: Forms through D2: 23; New paid teams: 1; Excluded: Unpaid, duplicate, invalid.\nCheck in simulator: Unpaid, duplicate, invalid.\nWhy: Forms are not paid bookings. Only captured and confirmed teams count.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1p5dgB1Wh8E_nYr3b2sRuFnGUaDykfjci/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"2e5604bf-875c-45dc-be90-1e551d04cd53","module_id":"03d4e523-70dc-43cb-bb14-d1028f8d3f49","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:40.619429+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:40.619429+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Set Ananya’s lab login","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Set a temporary training-system credential so we can perform the actual login test.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 07\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, ROOT\ns = connect(\"IAM-J-101\")\nu = find_user(s, \"ananya.shah\")\nassert u, \"STOP: create user first\"\nr = s.put(f\"{ROOT}/users/{u[''id'']}/reset-password\",\n    json={\"type\": \"password\", \"value\": \"AnanyaLab!2026\",\n          \"temporary\": False}, timeout=15)\nr.raise_for_status()\nprint(\"PASSWORD: local test credential saved\")\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nPASSWORD: local test credential saved\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nHTTP request completed without an error.\nConfirm login in the following portal test.\nNever record the password in evidence.\nUNDERSTAND:\nA successful password change is not proof of the right application access.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 35–36 (Guided task 07). Module 03 (Explain).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"2e89b580-3661-48a3-ace9-70f3c8fb3cc1","module_id":"fc3b345d-ea20-4ef5-8693-9796ed1939b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:06.547944+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:06.547944+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S26 - Create a verified-only GET API","content":"WHAT: We are retrieving approved resources from SQLite for the Grama website.\nDO: Insert listVerified() in db.js and connect the GET endpoint in server.js. Include source text in SQLite search and return only verified resources.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The GET API excludes pending suggestions; notice search returns GRC-001, GRC-002 and GRC-006.\nIF IT FAILS: Insert the helper before module.exports, export it, save the route, restart Express, then test.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 05 PowerPoint, task S26 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S26.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"2f8fb60d-0eb0-4fbd-8170-e8038f21dbe4","module_id":"cb186bda-f107-4d57-bf65-07aa218b21ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:48.292329+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:48.292329+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T42 - Reproduce, escalate and retest","content":"Work task T42: Reproduce, escalate and retest.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Issue desk in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Select mobile and reproduce the checkout error.\n2. Send a ticket naming the two failed records and exact error.\n3. Read the simulated engineer response and retest on mobile.\nCompleted example: Test device: Android mobile; Observed error: GATEWAY_TIMEOUT; Ticket: CA-BUG-02; Engineer response: WEB-FIX-02; Retest: Captured after simulated fix.\nCheck in simulator: Captured after simulated fix.\nWhy: The marketer reports evidence. The website team owns the code fix.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1p5dgB1Wh8E_nYr3b2sRuFnGUaDykfjci/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"45","lesson_id":"2f8fd13e-7960-42f4-8c3e-a81a60207e23","module_id":"03d4e523-70dc-43cb-bb14-d1028f8d3f49","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:42.33893+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:42.33893+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Map the IAM system and work cycle","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: See where the work travels before changing any account.\nWORKFLOW: Service Desk (request + approvals) → Keycloak (user + group) → Report Portal (allowed/denied application actions) → Review Queue (evidence + handover).\nFOLLOW THE CYCLE: Verify ticket → Find or create identity → Assign Finance-Viewers → Test View 200 and Edit 403 → Save observed evidence → Remove access after approved offboarding.\nCHECK: Each step has an input, system action and visible output. Stop if identity, approval or group is unclear.\nUNDERSTAND: An IAM group change is not enough. You must prove what the employee can and cannot do in the application.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 3–5. Module 01 (Engage).","duration":"25","lesson_id":"3150dfd1-3005-44a9-8fa1-a0d156389a6f","module_id":"e3fe24fa-601b-4db2-8e4a-d03421c93044","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:01.386974+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:01.386974+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Grade 7 Mathematics — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 7 Mathematics course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"3183e8e8-d9cc-4258-a1e6-f8e6e0815cb7","module_id":"0e64d452-bc0d-4894-bac5-8cf1b8c191cd","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:12.051574+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:12.051574+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"S17 - Import a backup safely","content":"WHAT: We are restoring JSON local drafts without accepting unverified public records.\nDO: Test real backup restoration: export; remove the saved drafts; import the JSON once; import it again.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Original draft IDs and six field values return on the first import; the second import creates zero duplicates.\nIF IT FAILS: Do not test restoration while the original drafts are still present.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 03 PowerPoint, task S17 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S17.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"33714c4f-4c4b-44d1-96c2-e88a622d9de5","module_id":"725cf25c-1179-43c1-92b8-a16610df08b7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:42.602915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:42.602915+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Engineering Units, Symbols and Calculations","content":"Recognise physical quantities, symbols and units, including mg/L and ppm. Prepare molarity and dilution calculations. Calculate pollutant loads using flow and concentration. Work through measurement variation, standard deviation and uncertainty, checking units throughout.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"33e89fd6-c460-4b6f-95ac-44c989510cc8","module_id":"1693896b-bc75-4181-9257-25bc84f4a651","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:34.647054+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:34.647054+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T36 - Check that ads are active","content":"Work task T36: Check that ads are active.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Review & publish.\n2. Press Complete ad review (training).\n3. See Active in the Delivery field.\nCompleted example: Review result: Approved; Delivery: Active (simulation).\nCheck in simulator: Active (simulation).\nWhy: An active label means the simulation is ready to play the results.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1izzDMQe1LDWcTfFFemfkzLiNafREVXsf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"15","lesson_id":"34187ca6-12e9-4a1a-87a2-524fe21e1d2f","module_id":"9d37547e-5aca-4397-a704-05c09a59cb3a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:38.640871+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:38.640871+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Write an evidence-based workplace update","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Use 17_Communication_Log to draft and track a clear owner/status message; verify any promised completion time against source evidence.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"3419980f-da09-4cbe-bf21-3ce93d2571d7","module_id":"067167c1-86b5-4777-b5a0-a4df453dd68c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:04.117758+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:04.117758+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Evaluate readiness and escalate blockers","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Record ticket reference, current status, missing response and day-one risk; escalate to the responsible IT or facility owner.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"3647d665-c8e1-4477-8c47-1f3115c813c5","module_id":"067167c1-86b5-4777-b5a0-a4df453dd68c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:03.551789+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:03.551789+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Trigger WARNING at 70C and keep it at 68C","content":"Use the same simulator to commit a valid 70C sample; expect WARNING and lamp ON. Next commit 68C; because the warning was already ON, the lamp must stay ON. Do not reset state between these linked cases. OUTPUT: two checked results showing warning activation and hysteresis.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"36f57981-d0b8-4789-95e3-5ee7cf9cb777","module_id":"68737413-f85b-4ebe-b5e4-4e4e1e5ad92b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:25.270964+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:25.270964+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Inspect Week 4 sales and channel evidence","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read SwaadFit_M5_Source.xlsx and distinguish objective trials, channel conversions and available cost data.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"370b7c82-9219-4c42-9afb-450334016839","module_id":"f555663a-aca5-4d75-b223-634f30c3762b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:48.28268+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:48.28268+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Read original stakeholder statements","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Inspect the supplied source statements and distinguish facts, preferences, rules and missing information.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"37158b14-1d67-475e-99d5-7d5a9be58527","module_id":"239ff18f-a7a8-4b28-b422-9dca596c667d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:17.867875+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:17.867875+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Score three customer patterns in Excel","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 2 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Use workbook 01_Score to compute weighted scores using Need 35 percent, Reach 25 percent, Repeat 25 percent and Size 15 percent.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"38172042-9d3d-4388-9a1e-a5feda4da9e4","module_id":"82d21194-c6d2-4f91-8a31-17f8e16bde2d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:37.763118+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:37.763118+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Explain: Course Setup and Lab Readiness","content":"MODULE 0: Course Setup and Lab Readiness\n6E STAGE: Explain\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\n1\n0:00–0:25\nUnderstand the business problem and identify required data.\n2\n0:25–1:05\nAudit and clean relevant sheets.\n3\n1:05–2:15\nBuild Excel formulas and PivotTables.\n4\n2:15–3:10\nInterpret Excel outputs and write initial findings.\n5\n3:10–4:35\nLoad Power BI data, create relationships and DAX.\n6\n4:35–5:20\nBuild the dashboard.\n7\n5:20–6:00\nComplete the conclusion and prepare to present.\n\nRESOURCE: M0_Course_Setup_Explain.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"386c5dc1-7e22-4ab3-89d4-e3b8f0fee4ac","module_id":"cf79daa7-c6cd-45ae-b28c-77635b6e983b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:13.296899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:13.296899+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T31 - Select placements in the Ad set","content":"Work task T31: Select placements in the Ad set.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Stay on the Ad sets screen.\n2. Tick Feed and Reels and inspect your four exported images.\n3. Press Mark placement check.\nCompleted example: Where: Ads Manager > Ad sets; Placement: Feed and Reels; Creatives: Four exported PNG files.\nCheck in simulator: Four exported PNG files.\nWhy: Audience, budget and placement belong together in the ad set for this exercise.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (not yet uploaded to Drive): Module_05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign/M05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign.pptx\nLMS ADMIN ACTION: Upload this module deck separately before learner publication.","duration":"25","lesson_id":"38bfcdf6-7ea2-470c-b0bb-17a1489ee213","module_id":"5e0d6e1b-e6fa-450d-93da-45fb48e4bcb7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:35.521524+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:35.521524+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"T34 - Reject wrong claims before launch","content":"Work task T34: Reject wrong claims before launch.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Ads Manager > Review.\n2. Press Run pre-launch checks. Read every failed fact if it stops you.\n3. Fix the wrong field or ad, then run the checks again.\nCompleted example: Check: Date, fee, age, city, URL; Ads: Both approved before review; If mismatch: STOP and correct.\nCheck in simulator: STOP and correct.\nWhy: Campaign safety means checking the words and the data, not just saving a draft.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1izzDMQe1LDWcTfFFemfkzLiNafREVXsf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"39194792-2bdd-49b2-ac93-13d546fce7e7","module_id":"9d37547e-5aca-4397-a704-05c09a59cb3a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:37.508383+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:37.508383+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Write the manager Situation Brief","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 1 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Complete workbook 05_Brief!B8:B12 using sales, research, price promotion and stock evidence; distinguish observed facts from possible causes.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"393c1bf8-1c8b-4886-97c5-4306f745fa96","module_id":"29687f58-184a-4af4-a628-043d14f5d175","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:35.216303+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:35.216303+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Open PowerShell, check tools and run 14 tests","content":"On a Windows computer, open PowerShell in the downloaded ECE_L1_RUN_ONLY folder. Run the course environment-check command shown in the M03 PowerPoint. Confirm Python and a supported C compiler are available. Then run the supplied C assessment runner against your edited source. If a tool is missing, follow the course recovery steps; do not invent a PASS. OUTPUT: actual 14-case test execution.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"39da312c-6562-4aac-9949-d2787bcac31c","module_id":"384d0feb-b2bd-4611-a17a-dba0f96c9ada","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:28.396087+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:28.396087+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Module 05 - Cow and Bird Digestion","content":"Follow the approved BODY QUEST slides 53-61 (9 slides). Pause to attempt every question in writing before checking the answer, use feedback, and retry where requested.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"3a1bf631-4e76-4242-993f-f1e25839efbd","module_id":"1358031d-1874-4cdc-99dd-282d6d1af544","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:58.494026+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:58.494026+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Respond to the competitor discount event","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 2 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: In 03_Change record which target and retail-message decisions stay or change after the competitor price update, explaining evidence for each.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"3c64cf15-5ef0-41c6-aae5-2548e348c95f","module_id":"82d21194-c6d2-4f91-8a31-17f8e16bde2d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:38.896561+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:38.896561+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Check the saved IAM configuration","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Independently verify that Ananya exists, is active and has the correct group.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 09\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe check_state.py guided-provision\nRUN / PERFORM:\nPowerShell: execute the command in iam_l1_lab.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nPASS | Account exists\nPASS | Correct active/inactive state\nPASS | Finance-Viewers membership\nPASS | No Finance-Editors membership\nSTATE CHECK: PASS\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nIf FAIL, fix the Keycloak state before continuing.\nThis checker does not prove portal permission.\nThe portal test is next.\nUNDERSTAND:\nThe checker reads saved Keycloak state instead of trusting our earlier print.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 39–40 (Guided task 09). Module 03 (Explain).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"3c7f6d5d-34fc-42e4-b790-ea7bf602e4fa","module_id":"fc3b345d-ea20-4ef5-8693-9796ed1939b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:07.116695+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:07.116695+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Reconcile the raw register to GL","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Inspect both exception documents. In 01_RECON, record the raw Rs 12,92,000 control, the September adjustments and ledger comparison; distinguish an October invoice from September revenue.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"3cdfcad0-3e53-4df1-852f-db459a661ff5","module_id":"256300bc-d9a5-4ac7-b553-8db9932a5b71","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:52.870316+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:52.870316+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4}]'::jsonb) r
