SELECT r."title", r."content", r."duration", r."lesson_id", r."module_id", r."created_at", r."updated_at", r."description", r."order_index"
FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"Complete Day 1 joining control records","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Update 05_Day1_Record with actual DOJ, arrival result, identity check, employee ID and HRIS status from verified evidence.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"3da6185b-af4c-47d0-b6ba-f1a4d01923ba","module_id":"022301cb-819a-4972-beb0-ed07f30a1312","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:06.116888+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:06.116888+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Reconcile Instagram platform and order counts","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 4 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: In 03_Reconcile compare 60 Instagram events with 52 completed and 8 cancelled orders; mark remaining definition and tagging checks.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"3e0bb25a-1cd4-49cb-8a5c-ad1dd6975d2b","module_id":"2563fa98-58f6-4862-80d8-934090fe4bad","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:46.292737+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:46.292737+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Express: Final Submission and Oral Defence","content":"MODULE 5: Final Submission and Oral Defence\n6E STAGE: Express\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nFINAL SUBMISSION SUMMARY\nProblem\n5 Findings\n3 Actions\nLimitation\n\nRESOURCE: M5_Final_Submission_Express.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M5_Express_Final_Submission_Builder.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M5_Express_Final_Submission_Builder.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18xivvriBMfh3msLth1r7RrpX8UNwIkx5/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"3e1d5a6c-c60c-4bc4-a9cb-2ef2ae0e49ac","module_id":"b7fb8dde-5329-4c61-8197-4f52cdf3ccac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:30.87389+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:30.87389+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S30 - Load live API resources into Grama","content":"WHAT: We are replacing static sample records with actual verified rows from Express.\nDO: Load verified resource cards from the live Express GET API instead of the static JavaScript sample.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Verified resource cards are displayed from SQLite; pending suggestions are not public.\nIF IT FAILS: Confirm the actual API response and Express restart if code changed.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 05 PowerPoint, task S30 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S30.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"3ec34f5b-61ec-4b4b-8887-18b0ee861108","module_id":"cb186bda-f107-4d57-bf65-07aa218b21ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:50.574966+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:50.574966+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Verify both offboarding approvals before revocation","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Verify that both Ananya’s and Rohit’s leaver instructions are authorized before changing either account.\nRUN FROM iam_l1_lab:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe approval_check.py IAM-L-301\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe approval_check.py IAM-L-401\nCHECK: Match the expected employee IDs, usernames and approved removal operation. If either approval fails, stop that request; do not revoke on an unverified instruction.\nPRESERVE: IAM-J-101 and IAM-J-201 joiner evidence were already saved. Keep these historical files unchanged.\nUNDERSTAND: Offboarding is a new authorized transaction, not an extension of the original provisioning approval.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 71–72. Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"25","lesson_id":"3ec38cb5-5534-463c-83cc-2867c52e4b75","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:13.075368+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:13.075368+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Receive the channel activation request","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 3 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Open the Module 3 deck and learner workbook from the ZIP. Note that allocated budget does not equal spending or manager approval.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"3f2b87a5-162f-42b6-95fc-008d03f38936","module_id":"7f78ef5d-704e-4360-9363-d268dc2a086e","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:40.320586+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:40.320586+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Inspect Day 7 updates and active issues","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read the source employee and manager notes plus earlier open Day 1 items before updating statuses.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"3f8b0165-ddf7-4f2b-bb9b-aeac3c663a5c","module_id":"fd462bb9-9a77-4355-ac64-2859a808c0f2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:08.680241+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:08.680241+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Write acceptance checks and check the register","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Finish M3_REQUIREMENTS!F12:F18 with measurable evidence checks, compare the worked S06 example and flag unclear items.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"40939520-bb8b-4fd2-95c5-d1b32bf8fe32","module_id":"239ff18f-a7a8-4b28-b422-9dca596c667d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:19.001965+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:19.001965+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Play: Predict Coin 10","content":"Open the offline Pattern Runner simulator and start Mission 01. Use Play, Next Coin and Replay to watch the lanes. Predict coin 10 before viewing the rule. If you miss, compare the earlier coin groups and try again.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"415f9ebc-6cda-41c5-90cf-76906f100952","module_id":"1e5dd0b7-4d92-4c1b-9680-7b1d66d63911","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:42.676279+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:42.676279+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Read the eight-section manager handover requirement","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Review what the operations manager needs: evidence, process finding, test outcome, pilot result, outstanding gap and recommendation.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"4244ba67-d433-485e-af3f-1e3166855393","module_id":"61953943-322d-4034-ad05-89c9b5a237af","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:28.710752+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:28.710752+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Commercial Readiness - Guided Learning and Practice","content":"Work through Tasks 31-35 with the module learning deck and operating workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"4252b4e9-2886-4208-9b6a-966e55f65799","module_id":"08a455ad-0829-4e80-9dc9-f173eb271eda","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:40.406998+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:40.406998+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T43 - Resume results and compare both ads","content":"Work task T43: Resume results and compare both ads.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Daily ad results in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Check full six-day clicks, spend and verified paid teams for A and B.\n2. Choose a careful action and explain it with evidence.\n3. Record that new spending needs manager approval.\nCompleted example: New days: D3, D4, D5, D6; Ad A: 7 paid • 210 clicks • ₹1,470; Ad B: 4 paid • 201 clicks • ₹1,420.\nCheck in simulator: 4 paid • 201 clicks • ₹1,420.\nWhy: A decision needs spend and booking evidence. We should not scale from a tiny sample without review.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1p5dgB1Wh8E_nYr3b2sRuFnGUaDykfjci/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"30","lesson_id":"42f5429d-ffdc-4e3f-9b4a-5511f94f93d9","module_id":"03d4e523-70dc-43cb-bb14-d1028f8d3f49","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:42.910147+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:42.910147+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Write the early-cycle manager handover","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; GrainGlow files are inside 04_Independent_Practice. Use this ZIP source to avoid mixing versions. Read 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the work.\nDO: Complete 06_Cycle_Note with seven evidence-grounded fields before opening any completed references.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"43ea09b2-dfe0-41d0-acc0-5ec24e8e86f7","module_id":"a97147bf-68b1-495a-b6d6-a3553e62ad46","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:53.693944+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:53.693944+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Investigate product margin deterioration","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 03_PRODUCTS: calculate realised unit prices, actual unit costs, budget and actual contribution margins, and product-level differences.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"446cb52c-672a-4272-99b9-e8a687b550e5","module_id":"5d6e6c3b-27f1-4069-9272-fb255d0feb98","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:55.989007+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:55.989007+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"T25 - Make a Meta-style Sales campaign","content":"Work task T25: Make a Meta-style Sales campaign.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Ads Manager (practice).\n2. Choose Sales as the objective.\n3. Press Create campaign.\nCompleted example: Objective: Sales; Campaign type: New campaign.\nCheck in simulator: New campaign.\nWhy: We want paid registrations, not just likes.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (not yet uploaded to Drive): Module_05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign/M05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign.pptx\nLMS ADMIN ACTION: Upload this module deck separately before learner publication.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"44904672-dd9d-4c97-b126-e537deed4054","module_id":"5e0d6e1b-e6fa-450d-93da-45fb48e4bcb7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:32.106059+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:32.106059+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Inspect the new batch source events","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read source candidate profiles, documents, setup requests, Day 1, check-ins, issues and probation decisions before writing any state.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"44d72fe4-46d1-44c8-ad64-cb12c1e2dbdd","module_id":"1a9397ae-439a-4b11-a6a7-a53ccaa97535","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:20.0219+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:20.0219+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Validate your next employee ticket","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Ticket IAM-J-201 is approved. Use the same method to onboard Rohit Nair.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 15\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user\ns = connect()\nassert find_user(s, \"rohit.nair\") is None, \"HOLD: exists\"\nprint(\"TICKET: IAM-J-201 | APPROVED\")\nprint(\"USER: rohit.nair | GROUP: Finance-Viewers\")\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nTICKET: IAM-J-201 | APPROVED\nUSER: rohit.nair | GROUP: Finance-Viewers\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nRohit Nair | EMP-1043\nEmail rohit.nair@example.test\nView allowed; edit forbidden.\nIf there is an existing identity, HOLD.\nUNDERSTAND:\nA new ticket reuses the same process; only approved employee data changes.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 56–57 (Guided task 15). Module 05 (Empower).","duration":"40","lesson_id":"450b9f5a-e1ec-4460-aa3e-00ce55a136b0","module_id":"6d083266-9280-4761-a335-079183e1eb66","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:10.521053+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:10.521053+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Write the Week 2 performance update","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 4 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Complete 04_Update with execution issue, channel evidence, unresolved count definition, next step and appropriate escalation.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"4657e014-069f-4fe8-910e-653f34095f6c","module_id":"2563fa98-58f6-4862-80d8-934090fe4bad","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:46.86414+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:46.86414+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Evolve: Course Setup and Lab Readiness","content":"MODULE 0: Course Setup and Lab Readiness\n6E STAGE: Evolve\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nDATA-QUALITY ISSUES YOU ARE EXPECTED TO NOTICE\nDocument treatment: Retain / Standardize / Exclude / Escalate.\n\nRESOURCE: M0_Course_Setup_Evolve.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M0_Evolve_Readiness_Exception_Decision_and_Recovery_Plan.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M0_Evolve_Readiness_Exception_Decision_and_Recovery_Plan.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1zFhoz_Bif5UtMS83s2UYb4L1YNDdOcOS/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"46e7fcec-2a04-42e9-8c6e-6c424a63afbc","module_id":"cf79daa7-c6cd-45ae-b28c-77635b6e983b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:14.351138+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:14.351138+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Forecast October to December and the full year","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 05_FCST using nine months of actual results and three forecast months; make forecast assumptions visible.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"70","lesson_id":"4772fa8c-8fad-45c6-b360-400c4fb025e4","module_id":"65f46751-f888-4cef-8899-82a916f8d88f","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:01.663952+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:01.663952+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T05 - Approve the campaign brief","content":"Work task T05: Approve the campaign brief.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Work order in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Check the event facts in Work order.\n2. Type Marketing Manager as the approver.\n3. Press Approve brief (training).\nCompleted example: Event: CLUTCH ARENA 5v5; Owner: Marketing Manager; Plan: 11 teams / ₹3,000 / 6 days.\nCheck in simulator: 11 teams / ₹3,000 / 6 days.\nWhy: We need the target, owner and spending limit before we make ads.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1qf78k8RvV7GgG3Rm725jIXzCtZ4LDmes/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"47a947ae-c323-47ac-91fe-99d12e1ea51e","module_id":"681f39c1-fc77-4026-b85b-29f1521668ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:19.612793+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:19.612793+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Draft the eight evidence-based handover sections","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete M7_HANDOVER!C11:C18 using exact verified results and ownership boundaries instead of copying the partial worked memo.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"70","lesson_id":"4a63b284-3f55-48ab-b1fc-513476a72b02","module_id":"61953943-322d-4034-ad05-89c9b5a237af","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:29.838787+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:29.838787+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"S07 - Add the second resource","content":"WHAT: We are adding another card so visitors can search different resources.\nDO: Add a second verified HTML resource card in index.html using the supplied GRC-001 record.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Two resources appear and the search input can distinguish them.\nIF IT FAILS: Inspect both card IDs and ensure no nested or unclosed HTML.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 02 PowerPoint, task S07 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S07.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"4aaf34a7-355e-43c4-a715-af6fecbd4d8f","module_id":"7a584fec-8468-485f-aad3-a5fe02e103ca","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:36.638291+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:36.638291+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Inspect setup requirements and responses","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read approved module source evidence by candidate, role and ticket or service-response status.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"4b426f02-d34e-40fa-bd5e-dbbbcb410f21","module_id":"067167c1-86b5-4777-b5a0-a4df453dd68c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:02.417461+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:02.417461+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Assemble the cycle manager handover","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 5 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Finish 04_Handover with M1 situation, M2 audience decision, M3 revised plan, M4 quality findings, M5 result and required approvals.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"65","lesson_id":"4bdf651b-f1a4-439f-9108-639f12ce77c4","module_id":"f555663a-aca5-4d75-b223-634f30c3762b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:50.573868+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:50.573868+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Explore New Trails and School Flags (optional presentation)","content":"Study the new Left, Centre and Right pattern and the school flag display. Predict first; use the later slides to compare your method with the worked explanation.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"4c0df298-18c0-4644-a175-5c1b5cc5cd46","module_id":"d4d7a7ff-2205-4fcc-bef4-f935f149d458","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:45.275877+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:45.275877+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Contaminant Transport and Mass Balances","content":"Learn how moving water carries pollutants and why a plume spreads. Compare advection, diffusion and dispersion. Calculate contaminant amounts entering, leaving or remaining in a system. Explore how contaminants attach to sediment and interpret simple partition values.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"4c21a4de-7898-4e0f-b185-9a2eda3db621","module_id":"681a8ddc-72a2-4bae-b74b-cfff0e69ecfd","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:25.126336+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:25.126336+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Grade 11 Political Science — Political Science","content":"Complete Grade 11 Political Science course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"4ceff225-88c8-4286-ab76-92c0ba0aa762","module_id":"bc4d5814-1044-4a68-bd72-7e4d824d30ef","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:52.243018+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:52.243018+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"S25 - Inspect stored SQLite records","content":"WHAT: We are reading the real database to confirm the Grama records were saved correctly.\nDO: Create the database inspection script and query the stored Grama resources.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Eight verified resources are visible with their expected IDs and fields.\nIF IT FAILS: Inspect the active SQLite path and table contents if count or status is wrong.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 04 PowerPoint, task S25 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S25.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"4d3c2595-ff6a-4330-853c-2bbe186ceae4","module_id":"8009900c-e018-4848-aab2-f1e19136e26a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:47.43526+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:47.43526+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Sampling Instruments and Laboratory Quality","content":"Choose sampling stations and understand representative samples. Learn the role of bottle labels, preservation and signed chain-of-custody records. Compare pH, DO and turbidity instruments and the readings they produce. Check blanks, duplicates and detection limits before reporting results.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"4d8bfefa-9eaa-4f5b-aa4a-12f7b08eed7f","module_id":"047e1821-ac42-4aa7-a021-38559df260ba","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:33.294299+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:33.294299+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Module 02 - Teeth Saliva and Starch Evidence","content":"Follow the approved BODY QUEST slides 14-31 (18 slides). Pause to attempt every question in writing before checking the answer, use feedback, and retry where requested.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"4e68016d-eae1-4ce7-a4bb-42c684652c8e","module_id":"952a7f6b-29ec-4c0e-b600-5049b3a90b06","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:56.937757+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:56.937757+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Reallocate the budget after manager change","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 3 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Record micro-creator unavailability; rebalance the remaining channels to the revised Rs 1,08,000 case plan without breaching protected minimums.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"4ed8d55a-a18b-4d5d-af7c-d90ebc08fdaa","module_id":"7f78ef5d-704e-4360-9363-d268dc2a086e","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:42.589905+00:0