FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"Independent assessment — Neha’s joiner ticket","content":"WORKPLACE MISSION: A NEW approved joiner ticket IAM-J-501 requests Finance-Viewers for Neha Iyer, username neha.iyer, EMP-1052.\nTHIS IS NOT AN I TRY VARIATION. Do not look for a completed solution or copy Rohit’s code unchanged.\nIMPLEMENT: Verify authorization and identity, choose the required account operations, create exactly the correct identity, grant only the approved viewer group, perform both portal actions and preserve ticket-linked joiner evidence.\nEXPECTED RESULT: Correct single account; Finance-Viewers present; Finance-Editors absent; View HTTP 200; Edit HTTP 403; accepted joiner evidence.\nCHECK / PROOF: Record observed evidence for IAM-J-501 before beginning Neha’s later leaver assessment.\nUNDERSTAND: This separate assessment tests whether you can apply the guided method to a new approved workplace request without the code solution.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 70. Module 05 (Empower).","duration":"90","lesson_id":"60595fec-f0f7-4013-9fc2-0d8dadef4921","module_id":"6d083266-9280-4761-a335-079183e1eb66","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:12.508402+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:12.508402+00:00","description":null,"order_index":9},{"title":"Record induction and unresolved blockers","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Continue 05_Day1_Record with access, equipment, policies, manager handover, open item and Day 1 result.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"60ec55ec-003a-49a9-8a49-6d6bb13e7b04","module_id":"022301cb-819a-4972-beb0-ed07f30a1312","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:06.683281+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:06.683281+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Measure the separate Week 2 transfer case","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; GrainGlow files are inside 04_Independent_Practice. Use this ZIP source to avoid mixing versions. Read 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the work.\nDO: Open GrainGlow_Independent_Transfer.pptx inside 04_Independent_Practice; fill 01_Analytics with verified channel metrics and confirmed trials.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"65","lesson_id":"616ab951-ac8b-4085-a172-9b986123f45c","module_id":"a97147bf-68b1-495a-b6d6-a3553e62ad46","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:54.258604+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:54.258604+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Reconcile October revenue and forecast differences","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 06_OCT_RECON: verify the posted ledger revenue and compare October revenue and EBITDA with forecast.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"61e72267-e6c6-43f0-877c-06b71b798a6f","module_id":"056822e1-887b-4a10-99e9-70f234cd58b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:05.360292+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:05.360292+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Read the pilot measurement questions","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Identify four separate evidence points: affected-order rate, confirmation time, late orders and refresh completion.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"62b5708a-4db6-4d5f-8308-bba3bc202676","module_id":"144a0889-2ac7-47f6-8cea-a450a7efd3f1","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:25.597602+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:25.597602+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Explore: Business Analytics","content":"MODULE 2: Business Analytics\n6E STAGE: Explore\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nBUSINESS ANALYTICS EXCEL STEPS\nFind duplicates in Order_ID.\nRemove both conflicting NR-10121 records from the dashboard dataset.\nCount blanks in Customer Satisfaction; leave missing satisfaction blank.\nCreate numeric return and complaint indicators.\nActual Hours\n(Stage_End - Stage_Start) * 24\nDelay Hours\nActual Hours - Expected_Hours\nExpected visuals: Delivery by Region | Return / Complaint Trend | Satisfaction Comparison | Delay by Stage.\n\nRESOURCE: M2_Business_Analytics_Explore.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"62c68556-bf44-433a-8489-e08c58c24cd0","module_id":"56bcb15d-8908-460a-9eb0-e8fe9461a59c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:19.621875+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:19.621875+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Water and Wastewater Treatment Processes","content":"Follow water through screens, settling tanks and filters. Explain coagulation, flocculation and a jar-test example. Compare activated-carbon adsorption with membrane separation. Learn how biological treatment and disinfection work and how to interpret removal and contact-time calculations.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"635c91d5-5d16-44ae-bdd4-baca2882141e","module_id":"f125e4a3-bf03-4ffd-8f22-384eff0f1725","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:36.006767+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:36.006767+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Record expected action, verdict and reason","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete the open test-case rows in M5_VALIDATION!E11:E18 and G11:H18; preserve the worked T04 example.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"65","lesson_id":"6472f294-82b8-4b7d-9dd1-f2f5c9912791","module_id":"3df6a56d-ec9f-466e-a689-aa94bd08320a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:23.607224+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:23.607224+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Engage: HR Analytics","content":"MODULE 3: HR Analytics\n6E STAGE: Engage\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nHR\nHR TASK\nIs workforce, recruitment or onboarding evidence signalling capacity / retention risk?\nUse these sheets\n08_HR_Workforce_Data\n09_HR_Recruitment_Funnel\n10_HR_Role_JD_Data\n11_HR_Onboarding_Perf\nCalculate workforce signals\nExit Rate, OT per Employee, Absence per Employee, Engagement and Vacancies.\nCalculate recruitment and onboarding signals\nOffer Acceptance, Joining Rate and 30-Day Check Rate.\n\nRESOURCE: M3_HR_Engage.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"65bb7d96-7c9e-4df8-925b-0643e316a9cc","module_id":"8759a2fe-d783-4917-9716-d5383a2387ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:22.492198+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:22.492198+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"S04 - Fit a small phone","content":"WHAT: We are adapting the same page to a 390-pixel phone screen.\nDO: Add a responsive CSS media query in styles.css and use Chrome DevTools at 390px width.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The same page fits a small phone and has no sideways scrolling.\nIF IT FAILS: Confirm the media query is saved, then inspect at the correct viewport width.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 01 PowerPoint, task S04 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S04.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"6617675a-3f32-42e8-a163-fd81f083fa23","module_id":"94232a37-0467-4fbc-bb04-b11c3a6b98ab","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:34.647552+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:34.647552+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S40 - Protect offline cache scope","content":"WHAT: We are keeping static Grama pages cached but excluding API and coordinator data.\nDO: Constrain the service-worker cache to static client files; exclude API, login, session and coordinator responses.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Static pages can be cached without making protected API responses available offline.\nIF IT FAILS: Inspect Cache Storage and Network to confirm private routes are excluded.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 07 PowerPoint, task S40 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S40.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"6674ac8a-1007-4abc-8335-4b6eb7456368","module_id":"f2a32bfe-3e30-4928-ab08-81ec0f90db87","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:56.838068+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:56.838068+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"S34 - Keep local backups private","content":"WHAT: We are ensuring browser backups contain LOCAL DRAFT entries only.\nDO: Restrict JSON backup exports to device-local draft entries; exclude server-only suggestions and coordinator records.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Export contains local drafts only, with no session, user or published database data.\nIF IT FAILS: Inspect downloaded JSON before recording PASS.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 05 PowerPoint, task S34 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S34.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"66b8f98c-6859-4024-a7b7-e651151ff374","module_id":"cb186bda-f107-4d57-bf65-07aa218b21ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:52.854758+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:52.854758+00:00","description":null,"order_index":9},{"title":"S09 - Render cards from data","content":"WHAT: We are making JavaScript generate resource cards instead of relying on hard-coded articles.\nDO: Remove BOTH hard-coded card articles from index.html; then finish all parts of the render() code in app.js before checking results.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Exactly two JavaScript-generated cards appear AFTER the renderer and both files are saved.\nIF IT FAILS: Do not refresh and expect two cards between the HTML removal and the final render() slide.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 02 PowerPoint, task S09 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S09.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"6756e36b-288e-44ce-9ea9-8e0820fb13a0","module_id":"7a584fec-8468-485f-aad3-a5fe02e103ca","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:37.771159+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:37.771159+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Read the probation decision and closure boundaries","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Study why proposed, approved, communicated and closed outcomes are different statuses and extension may remain active.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"67621352-a366-481c-ad76-c0f3251f8113","module_id":"77df4865-88d1-4fb4-9b03-948bf7a87499","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:16.327732+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:16.327732+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"S32 - Submit for coordinator review","content":"WHAT: We are sending a suggestion to the API without automatically approving it.\nDO: Submit the visitor suggestion form to the API for coordinator review without publishing the record.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The API returns a pending suggestion ID; it does not appear in verified public cards.\nIF IT FAILS: Check the POST response, all six fields and server-side validation.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 05 PowerPoint, task S32 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S32.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"6787ee27-0d9d-435c-ac21-17dfa2aed62b","module_id":"cb186bda-f107-4d57-bf65-07aa218b21ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:51.718424+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:51.718424+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"S44 - Create an independent Nila application","content":"WHAT: Build a new application for a different client without copying the Grama code.\nDO: Create a NEW empty Nila application using the eight-record Nila_Workshop_Client_Data.csv. Independently demonstrate design, frontend, Express, SQLite, protected review and evidence against the Nila assessment gates.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Assess against the 10 independent gates; withhold WS-104 because source_note is blank; record assistance honestly.\nIF IT FAILS: Do not copy Grama source or claim assessment PASS without independent assessor evidence.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 08 PowerPoint, task S44 (original V25 teaching content).\nCLIENT DATA: Nila_Workshop_Client_Data.csv: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GE45Hpdea-VTibbbkeov-1wnuAo4r_7u/view?usp=drivesdk\nASSESSMENT EVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S44_NILA_INDEPENDENT and NILA_CLIENT_ACCEPTANCE.","duration":"180","lesson_id":"67967b34-13bb-404c-97ca-8bae8bc58dc0","module_id":"92e65646-61c0-44a9-b3dd-8ecc8fb92dae","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:59.385685+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:59.385685+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Clear the warning and test an invalid sensor","content":"Continue the same controller state: commit 65C valid to clear the warning; expect NORMAL and lamp OFF. Later submit a sample marked INVALID; expect FAULT and lamp ON even if the displayed temperature is low. OUTPUT: checked clear, fault and recovery cases.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"67c9da0f-036c-463b-949d-157be2af3504","module_id":"68737413-f85b-4ebe-b5e4-4e4e1e5ad92b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:25.838722+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:25.838722+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Check the validation evidence and handoff","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Compare with CHECK_YOUR_WORK only after attempting; save the validation log, corrective action and retest decision.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"25","lesson_id":"694b4f93-ef6e-4323-8ceb-42ba2fc51699","module_id":"3df6a56d-ec9f-466e-a689-aa94bd08320a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:24.737862+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:24.737862+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Understand document-status rules","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Study complete, pending and issue states; understand why incomplete documents cannot be recorded as verified.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"6959de2d-3791-43b3-b46c-72bac9d3c857","module_id":"a698052a-6425-4f3f-abc5-71ed1fc1f9cf","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:59.29229+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:59.29229+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Compare forecast with the annual budget","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Use 05_FY_REVIEW to calculate the annual EBITDA and operating-cash planning gaps. Do not describe modeled operating cash as bank balance.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"69feaed6-5ead-4a07-ac3c-2ac1402f1b58","module_id":"65f46751-f888-4cef-8899-82a916f8d88f","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:02.236941+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:02.236941+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Validate the formula-driven onboarding dashboard","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Use 16_Dashboard to confirm joining records, confirmed/extended statuses, closed onboarding and open-issue counts, then hand over anomalies.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"6a45a8a9-2ad1-40d0-8046-83622fee3ec4","module_id":"77df4865-88d1-4fb4-9b03-948bf7a87499","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:18.592938+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:18.592938+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Empower: Course Setup and Lab Readiness","content":"MODULE 0: Course Setup and Lab Readiness\n6E STAGE: Empower\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nPOWER BI WORKFLOW\nLoad → Clean → Model → Measures → Visuals → Slicers\n\nRESOURCE: M0_Course_Setup_Empower.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"6d12c5c5-3b38-4572-9b85-752ae714dcc3","module_id":"cf79daa7-c6cd-45ae-b28c-77635b6e983b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:14.876724+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:14.876724+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Record the Day 60 follow-up evidence","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 06_Followup_Checkins for Day 60 with supported observations, open item, owner and next action.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"6e038dbf-245b-4ef3-b842-f0d903ebad43","module_id":"1d7fb1bb-786e-440a-8117-c59e29b8dda2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:14.910538+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:14.910538+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T23 - Create links that tell us which ad worked","content":"Work task T23: Create links that tell us which ad worked.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Tracking lab in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Fill the UTM link builder.\n2. Press Build A + B links.\n3. Check that A and B have different utm_content values.\nCompleted example: Source: meta; Medium: paid_social; Campaign: clutch_arena_6d; Ad A: squad_ad; Ad B: challenge_ad.\nCheck in simulator: challenge_ad.\nWhy: These labels help us see which ad brought a visitor.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1XAIeg9OHnwXONsTjITRLTCOmoFZ4ZXi8/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"25","lesson_id":"6e216432-23c0-451b-a536-3d669d544e7a","module_id":"8f675f68-d87b-40ab-aeff-7026a8b062ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:30.69222+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:30.69222+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Module 04 - Intestinal Villi and Nutrient Absorption","content":"Follow the approved BODY QUEST slides 43-52 (10 slides). Pause to attempt every question in writing before checking the answer, use feedback, and retry where requested.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"6e342b18-040e-49ac-93e3-fd4c82f9994c","module_id":"7fcc603a-1806-47cd-8f1e-96e44b80e6cc","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:57.974712+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:57.974712+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Diagnose GrainGlow launch and choose the customer","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; GrainGlow files are inside 04_Independent_Practice. Use this ZIP source to avoid mixing versions. Read 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the work.\nDO: Independently complete 03_Situation and 04_Target, using the new outlet cutoff and fresh coded ratings rather than SwaadFit answers.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"70","lesson_id":"6f97a219-f787-40ce-976d-e0b3a00411d9","module_id":"a97147bf-68b1-495a-b6d6-a3553e62ad46","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:52.559378+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:52.559378+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Submit the Target and Strategy Decision","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 2 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Complete 04_Handover; check objective, segment, positioning and price-response boundaries only after finishing your own evidence-based wording.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"7004a48e-4581-45ff-81f0-c616c678587c","module_id":"82d21194-c6d2-4f91-8a31-17f8e16bde2d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:39.468389+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:39.468389+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"T33 - Finish advertisement B and save draft","content":"Work task T33: Finish advertisement B and save draft.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Ads Manager → Ads. Save Ad B name and its tracking link.\n2. Attach exported B Feed and B Reel PNG files from Asset Library.\n3. Check both images, then save the two-ad draft.\nCompleted example: Ad name: CA_CHALLENGE_AD; Creative: B; URL label: utm_content=challenge_ad.\nCheck in simulator: utm_content=challenge_ad.\nWhy: Both ads must be ready before the manager reviews them.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (not yet uploaded to Drive): Module_05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign/M05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign.pptx\nLMS ADMIN ACTION: Upload this module deck separately before learner publication.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"7017d3f0-72a5-4614-8c5c-baf446871444","module_id":"5e0d6e1b-e6fa-450d-93da-45fb48e4bcb7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:36.655208+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:36.655208+00:00","description":null,"order_index":9},{"title":"Prove Ananya’s login is blocked","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Check the saved state and then attempt a brand-new login as the disabled user.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 23\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe check_state.py guided-revoke\nRUN / PERFORM:\nPowerShell: run checker; then attempt the new login.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nSTATE CHECK: PASS\nNew login as ananya.shah -> REJECTED\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nOpen a NEW private browser window.\nGo to http://127.0.0.1:5000.\nTry Ananya with her lab credentials.\nA new authenticated portal session must NOT start.\nUNDERSTAND:\nRevocation must be proven, not assumed. This test does not prove all old enterprise sessions are invalid.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 77–78 (Guided task 23). Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"707fbb42-2cd3-465b-8e6a-512a4608f9c0","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:14.211185+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:14.211185+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Reject an unapproved editor request","content":"BEFORE THE HOLD TASK: Run .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe approval_check.py IAM-X-202. Expected decision is HOLD because the application owner has not approved Finance-Editors. Do not change any access.\n\nWHAT WE ARE DOING: IAM-X-202 says “add Finance-Editors urgently” but has NO owner approval. Do not grant it.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 20\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom approval_check import inspect\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, group_names\ncheck = inspect(\"IAM-X-202\")\nassert check[\"decision\"] == \"HOLD\", \"STOP: approval status changed\"\ns = connect()\nu = find_user(s, check[\"username\"])\nassert u, \"STOP: missing employee\"\ngroups = group_names(s, u[\"id\"])\nassert \"Finance-Editors\" not in groups, \"STOP: prohibited grant exists\"\nprint(\"HOLD IAM-X-202: approval is missing\")\nprint(\"EDITOR GROUP PRESENT:\", \"Finance-Editors\" in groups)\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nHOLD IAM-X-202: approval is missing\nEDITOR GROUP PRESENT: False\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nNo state-changing command is executed.\nRohit is still viewer-only.\nRecord HOLD and route for approval.\nUNDERSTAND:\nIn IAM, refusing an unauthorized change is a real security action.\nNEXT STEP / EVIDENCE:\nAfter the no-change check, run .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe route_hold.py IAM-X-202 and verify the IAM-APPROVALS queue receipt.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 68–69 (Guided task 20). Module 05 (Empower).","duration":"40","lesson_id":"70f9db63-fc0b-4b8a-b37c-c11ebe5d4b25","module_id":"6d083266-9280-4761-a335-079183e1eb66","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:12.224316+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:12.224316+00:00","description":null,"order_index":8},{"title":"Receive the supermarket BA investigation","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder. COURSE SOURCE FOLDER: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1qvUnv2aLPCAxFulPzM18me34r_n146Jj.\nDO: Understand that walk-in and WhatsApp orders share shelf stock; identify the business question and open the guided slide-to-workbook route.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"714d8a41-a8d2-46a5-98a6-81fe984c1b7c","module_id":"9184ac19-93a3-42ea-90f1-0de8006dab18","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:11.045964+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:11.045964+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Study a manager-ready evidence statement","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Review the worked manager report example and distinguish amount, business meaning, source and proposal.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"72927c41-b5df-424c-b818-013c2d46d522","module_id":"d61fd402-a087-41e8-bb8c-b4021a36f869","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:07.344488+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:07.344488+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Reallocate and draft a new marketing activation","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; GrainGlow files are inside 04_Independent_Practice. Use this ZIP source to avoid mixing versions. Read 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the work.\nDO: Respond to the Rs 54,000 budget cap and creator unavailability. Complete 05_Activation and 07_Creative_Execution with owner, CTA and approval.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"70","lesson_id":"72a99069-9481-48dd-8a27-32278b318ce8","module_id":"a97147bf-68b1-495a-b6d6-a3553e62ad46","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:53.126229+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:53.126229+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Record the calculations and number-line working","content":"Use the workbook as your working record. Calculate each day from the 0.5 GB class and 0.3 GB revision-video samples. Subtract each neighbouring amount, compare with the 1.5 GB daily allowance, and predict the next positions when moving three units left.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"72e7f160-caff-4a11-816f-9c7b7af96ede","module_id":"fe9bc26e-1335-4f8c-a602-73bd583e43f5","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:52.261829+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:52.261829+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Receive the customer priority decision","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 2 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Open the Module 2 guided deck and workbook from 01_Learner_Modules in the integrated ZIP; understand the Marketing Manager request for four-week customer priority.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"73bb9fa2-a15c-4f88-be78-1bf17767f55e","module_id":"82d21194-c6d2-4f91-8a31-17f8e16bde2d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:36.634418+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:36.634418+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Power BI Core Foundation — Complete Guided Lesson","content":"Use the attached 121-slide Power BI Core Foundation presentation. Follow the 18-step learning loop: Frame (1-4), Locate + Do (5-9), See + Prove (10-13), Recover + Transfer (14-18).\n\nTOPICS:\nP1. Power BI workspace and views\nP2. Get Data from Excel\nP3. Power Query cleaning and data types\nP4. Merge vs Append\nP5. Fact tables, dimensions and star schema\nP6. Relationships and duplicate-key blockers\nP7. Date table\nP8. Calculated columns vs measures and DAX syntax\nP9. Total Revenue measure and Card\nP10. COUNTROWS vs DISTINCTCOUNT\nP11. DIVIDE and rate measures\nP12. Filter context and CALCULATE\nP13. SUMX and row-by-row expressions\nP14. Business measures\nP15. Core report visuals\nP16. Table, Matrix, Slicer, filters and interactions\nP17. Assemble and validate one report page\nP18. Final independent Power BI challenge\n\nPractice workbook named in the slides: Power_BI_Core_Practice_Data_and_Instructions.xlsx (not supplied with the current uploads). The uploaded NovaRetail Data Set.xlsx belongs to the separate MBA analytics lab and is not an exact replacement.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"741060f9-6d8d-4710-929f-b0dee40e6c08","module_id":"5a0cc0ce-c557-4837-af90-91748b29a908","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:09.031637+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:09.031637+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"HR & Workforce - Guided Learning and Practice","content":"Work through Tasks 20-24 with the module learning deck and operating workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"74e524a5-97d9-4222-ad41-b8c0e9e22583","module_id":"d8ee9236-6cd5-4abe-b991-9641086f6469","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:38.082149+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:38.082149+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Practise the first mystery and check the evidence","content":"Open the standalone Module 01 HTML offline. Enter a learner name or code; examine the advertisement and phone log, calculate all planned values and required differences, move the number-line token, correct mistakes and export your evidence record.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"7582c655-2861-4016-adb1-3ea7dc3abf99","module_id":"fe9bc26e-1335-4f8c-a602-73bd583e43f5","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:52.777803+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:52.777803+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3}]'::jsonb) r
