FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"Assess pilot readiness and remaining gaps","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Consider the 4.775 minute weighted time, two late orders and 94.3 percent refresh completion; record evidence-based pilot decision in M6_PILOT!B27.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"7589e5f1-8b7d-405a-8a6e-0f0b43b83cfd","module_id":"144a0889-2ac7-47f6-8cea-a450a7efd3f1","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:27.293982+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:27.293982+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Explore: Course Setup and Lab Readiness","content":"MODULE 0: Course Setup and Lab Readiness\n6E STAGE: Explore\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nWHAT YOU MUST SUBMIT AT THE END OF 6 HOURS\nExcel working file\nCleaning, formulas, minimum 2 PivotTables and one dashboard.\nPower BI file\nModel, KPI measures, one dashboard and working slicers.\nConclusion\n5 findings, 3 recommendations and 1 limitation.\nOral defence\nDefend the findings, evidence and recommended actions.\n\nRESOURCE: M0_Course_Setup_Explore.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"75e12f07-6a61-4c42-94db-902704a240ed","module_id":"cf79daa7-c6cd-45ae-b28c-77635b6e983b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:12.776316+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:12.776316+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Calculate achievement against the Week 4 goal","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 5 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: In 01_Result check 242 unique trials versus 230 target, enter the 12-trial variance percentage and confirm channel shares.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"76358d28-b9d6-4082-af07-27fce0c4bcd1","module_id":"f555663a-aca5-4d75-b223-634f30c3762b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:48.850217+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:48.850217+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Procurement & Materials - Guided Learning and Practice","content":"Work through Tasks 25-30 with the module learning deck and operating workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"769482d2-7b47-4308-818d-4a9836740a8e","module_id":"61e8ab43-9061-414b-97b6-0313ad79461a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:39.253054+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:39.253054+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Evolve: Final Submission and Oral Defence","content":"MODULE 5: Final Submission and Oral Defence\n6E STAGE: Evolve\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nFINAL SELF-CHECK BEFORE SUBMISSION\nCleaning done\nFormulas correct\nPivotTables done\nPower BI complete\n5 findings\n3 actions\n\nRESOURCE: M5_Final_Submission_Evolve.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M5_Evolve_Oral_Defence_Final_Quality_Gate.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M5_Evolve_Oral_Defence_Final_Quality_Gate.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1H0kk63DbTTHlVFaCn_X-4qO3gGq7_B9f/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"7702e6a0-a6a9-4c07-975f-3f5fad314be4","module_id":"b7fb8dde-5329-4c61-8197-4f52cdf3ccac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:31.393571+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:31.393571+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"S15 - Prepare an enquiry","content":"WHAT: We are preparing an enquiry message for a verified resource without sending it.\nDO: Add the prepared resource enquiry message and its editable textarea; do not implement sending.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: A resource-specific message is generated and can be edited; no message is sent.\nIF IT FAILS: If the text cannot be edited, check for an unintended readonly attribute.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 03 PowerPoint, task S15 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S15.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"77a50b09-cae1-4965-b109-5056d1865619","module_id":"725cf25c-1179-43c1-92b8-a16610df08b7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:41.459941+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:41.459941+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Show the mathematical proof in the workbook","content":"Record every neighbouring subtraction and explain why a row is or is not an Arithmetic Progression. Complete M2-P1, M2-P2 and M2-P3 independently before checking later teaching slides.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"77cd79c2-336f-4f89-b137-620a7f1ffec8","module_id":"307d06a3-fea2-4ab1-8c05-797ce3df083c","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:54.58233+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:54.58233+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"T15 - Plan the campaign","content":"Work task T15: Plan the campaign.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ad research in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Fill the plan form using the completed example.\n2. Press Save campaign plan.\n3. Check the plan summary.\nCompleted example: Objective: Sales; Ad sets: 1; Advertisements: 2; Days: 6; Budget: ₹3,000.\nCheck in simulator: ₹3,000.\nWhy: A simple plan helps us build the correct account setup.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1H-5eW5OhpLbO7DsFnlyXWDHHny8-3LO1/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"25","lesson_id":"784f0984-898e-41b8-b8fd-4e5b52c1400f","module_id":"f2f23969-4104-4df2-a4a8-d8687fad4dc6","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:25.856308+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:25.856308+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Verify Rohit’s new approved ticket","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Treat each employee request as a separate authorized transaction.\nRUN BEFORE CREATING THE ACCOUNT:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe approval_check.py IAM-J-201\nCHECK: Rohit Nair is EMP-1043, username rohit.nair, requested permission Finance-Viewers only. Ensure no existing duplicate identity. Previous Ananya approval does not authorize Rohit.\nUNDERSTAND: The same technical workflow is reused, but the right to perform it comes from the new approved ticket.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 54–55. Module 05 (Empower).","duration":"25","lesson_id":"79b8d9eb-de3d-48ad-be02-b45e09e6b0ab","module_id":"6d083266-9280-4761-a335-079183e1eb66","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:09.953684+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:09.953684+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T18 - Choose the tracking source","content":"Work task T18: Choose the tracking source.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Tracking lab in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Tracking lab.\n2. Choose CLUTCH_ARENA_WEB.\n3. Press Save data source.\nCompleted example: Site data source: CLUTCH_ARENA_WEB; Events: PageView, InitiateCheckout, Purchase.\nCheck in simulator: PageView, InitiateCheckout, Purchase.\nWhy: We must check events from the right tournament website.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1XAIeg9OHnwXONsTjITRLTCOmoFZ4ZXi8/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"7a5c064a-1fa9-4f26-823c-5d8e7a5b68e3","module_id":"8f675f68-d87b-40ab-aeff-7026a8b062ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:27.839776+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:27.839776+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Summarize customer patterns from research","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 1 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Use workbook customer research tab to name Patterns B and C from observed needs; do not invent a segment label unsupported by the response summary.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"7b3ed6c6-f33c-46f2-bd71-733dd0443ba8","module_id":"29687f58-184a-4af4-a628-043d14f5d175","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:34.084259+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:34.084259+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"T38 - Check the money left after Day 2","content":"Work task T38: Check the money left after Day 2.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Daily ad results in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Look at the Day 1 and Day 2 spend records.\n2. Subtract total spend from ₹3,000.\n3. Enter the amount left and check your work.\nCompleted example: Maximum budget: ₹3,000; Spent by Day 2: ₹950; Still available: ₹2,050.\nCheck in simulator: ₹2,050.\nWhy: Money left changes each day. Do not use the final six-day total yet.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1izzDMQe1LDWcTfFFemfkzLiNafREVXsf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"7b80b69b-d163-4a15-98b6-9884f029c93b","module_id":"9d37547e-5aca-4397-a704-05c09a59cb3a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:39.772653+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:39.772653+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"T22 - Check a failed payment makes no Purchase","content":"Work task T22: Check a failed payment makes no Purchase.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Tracking lab in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Press Failed payment test.\n2. Look at the event log.\n3. Confirm no new Purchase was added.\nCompleted example: Failed attempt: Recorded; Extra Purchase: 0.\nCheck in simulator: 0.\nWhy: Counting a failed payment would make the campaign report wrong.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1XAIeg9OHnwXONsTjITRLTCOmoFZ4ZXi8/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"7c5e9b74-dcfe-4d44-9cb3-9877f177397b","module_id":"8f675f68-d87b-40ab-aeff-7026a8b062ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:30.1238+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:30.1238+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Understand the design assignment and constraints","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Read the manager need and the three frozen decision rules before proposing a new way to confirm orders.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"7c8ab03e-0a2a-46b7-93a1-77d437c0a495","module_id":"4ebcf693-3bd3-4361-805c-aab771f99ee8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:19.852935+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:19.852935+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T32 - Finish advertisement A","content":"Work task T32: Finish advertisement A.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Ads Manager → Ads. Save Ad A name and its tracking link.\n2. In Asset Library, attach your exported A Feed and A Reel PNG files.\n3. Look at the actual attached images. Save Ad A.\nCompleted example: Ad name: CA_SQUAD_AD; Creative: A; URL label: utm_content=squad_ad.\nCheck in simulator: utm_content=squad_ad.\nWhy: The tracking link must match the creative it belongs to.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (not yet uploaded to Drive): Module_05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign/M05_Build_the_Ad_Campaign.pptx\nLMS ADMIN ACTION: Upload this module deck separately before learner publication.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"7d720dbe-15e4-431e-bd8b-4864e470d206","module_id":"5e0d6e1b-e6fa-450d-93da-45fb48e4bcb7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:36.0884+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:36.0884+00:00","description":null,"order_index":8},{"title":"S27 - Submit pending suggestions via API","content":"WHAT: We are saving a suggestion in SQLite as pending rather than publishing it.\nDO: Insert addSuggestion() into db.js and expose the POST suggestion endpoint. Apply exact field limits: title 80, category 40, village 60, place 120, hours 80 and source 160.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Valid submissions are stored as pending; invalid/overlong values are rejected without a new row.\nIF IT FAILS: Save the helper, export and route before restarting Express and sending the provided PowerShell request.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 05 PowerPoint, task S27 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S27.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"7d78f0fa-85ff-4a2e-a2c1-5f282234076d","module_id":"cb186bda-f107-4d57-bf65-07aa218b21ef","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:48.860128+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:48.860128+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Send a grounded manager status update","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Use 17_Communication_Log and 02_Onboarding_Tracker to summarize readiness, blockers, owner and next check without claiming closure.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"7d8f11d1-52fb-4d17-8505-40bcd22a3451","module_id":"0e53e3e2-0adb-4d30-b8ff-50c1399923f8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:12.922897+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:12.922897+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Module 03 - Digestive Journey and Peristalsis","content":"Follow the approved BODY QUEST slides 32-42 (11 slides). Pause to attempt every question in writing before checking the answer, use feedback, and retry where requested.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"7dbc7acf-5cb3-45c4-b92f-dbd51604cab4","module_id":"0986deb7-ba97-453f-a89f-33bd9e967cfa","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:57.460353+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:57.460353+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T19 - Test the page visit event","content":"Work task T19: Test the page visit event.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Tracking lab in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Press Visit page in Tracking lab.\n2. Look for PageView in the event table.\n3. Then check your task.\nCompleted example: Test button: Visit page; Expected event: PageView.\nCheck in simulator: PageView.\nWhy: PageView means a page was opened, not that someone paid.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1XAIeg9OHnwXONsTjITRLTCOmoFZ4ZXi8/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"15","lesson_id":"7e809a81-114f-4888-86c4-b88ba999297c","module_id":"8f675f68-d87b-40ab-aeff-7026a8b062ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:28.407108+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:28.407108+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"T48 - Prepare a traceable training handover","content":"Work task T48: Prepare a traceable training handover.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Final report in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Final report > Handover.\n2. Set the recipient, work order and verify the final record count.\n3. Send the training package and check the simulated receipt. Next, complete the new case.\nCompleted example: Recipient: Tournament organiser (simulated); Work order: CA-001; Package: 16 safe IDs and final report; Acceptance: Simulated receipt; not a real person.\nCheck in simulator: Simulated receipt; not a real person.\nWhy: A button does not prove an actual manager accepted the work. Do not claim real approval.\nAfter T48, complete CA-002 independently and export your practice evidence.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/17IglBQnnnIL9v2w0psRL_Vp2qeuQIzWf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"40","lesson_id":"7ef9405f-93bd-44d9-aec1-bfd7eca5d1e6","module_id":"216fd3f2-3bed-47da-be6f-5611e637a457","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:46.054313+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:46.054313+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"See and copy a NORMAL test at 60C","content":"Enter a simulated 60C valid sensor sample. Click WRITE TEMP, WRITE FLAGS, COMMIT and CHECK MY RESULT in the shown order. Expect NORMAL and the lamp OFF. Understand: TEMP_DC=600 represents 60.0C; COMMIT asks the controller model to evaluate the saved sample. OUTPUT: a checked NORMAL result.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"7fd65701-aadf-4d8d-a73d-a74bbce031b5","module_id":"68737413-f85b-4ebe-b5e4-4e4e1e5ad92b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:24.702335+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:24.702335+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Review L1 capability evidence","content":"FINAL L1 CAPABILITY CHECK: Can you inspect a real ticket and approval record; select the correct approved identity and group; run the required IAM operations; demonstrate allowed and denied application actions; detect and safely recover from a common failure; preserve joiner evidence before later revocation; and complete an unfamiliar ticket with a reviewer handover?\nREQUIRED OUTPUTS: Approved ticket context, actual account and permission states, application test evidence, separate joiner/leaver records and queue receipts for review.\nNOT YET CERTIFIED: Finishing the deck or obtaining a queue receipt alone does not establish job readiness. Full live Keycloak/browser verification, accessible reference recordings and unassisted first-time learner testing remain publication gates for the source v8 course.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 89–90. Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"8015c2ae-5bf6-4908-9d20-ef3848f52681","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:16.204314+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:16.204314+00:00","description":null,"order_index":11},{"title":"Prepare VS Code, PowerShell, Docker and recovery checks","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Make the Windows laptop ready for the later real IAM lab. The lab continues across Modules 02–06; do not duplicate or reset it.\n1. Extract the full learner package; locate the iam_l1_lab folder. Do not run scripts from inside a ZIP viewer.\n2. In VS Code choose File → Open Folder → iam_l1_lab. Select Terminal → New Terminal. Confirm the terminal is in that folder.\n3. Start Docker Desktop and verify its engine says Running. Check Python and Docker with:\npy --version\ndocker --version\ndocker compose version\n4. From iam_l1_lab run:\ndocker compose up -d\ndocker compose ps\nEXPECTED RESULT: The tools print installed version numbers; Keycloak shows as running. Output version text may differ from the example.\nCHECK / RECOVERY: Run Get-Location for a wrong folder; start Docker Desktop if engine is unavailable; inspect docker compose logs keycloak --tail 40 if Keycloak does not load. Use the .venv Python and install app requirements if a Python module is missing.\nUNDERSTAND: The offline simulator works on lower-resource computers, but it does not replace the real Docker/Keycloak lab. Minimum Windows/WSL/virtualization prerequisites must be checked first.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 14–18. Module 01 (Engage).","duration":"75","lesson_id":"81051f3f-0c57-439c-94ec-06925f7eb3fa","module_id":"e3fe24fa-601b-4db2-8e4a-d03421c93044","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:02.81185+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:02.81185+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Inspect YTD actuals, drivers and action assumptions","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read YTD_ACTUALS, OCT_DEC_DRIVERS, ANNUAL_BUDGET, ACTION_INPUTS and ACTION_TRACKER_INPUT without replacing sources with estimates.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"81784f0e-187e-49c9-8abd-eb0161f7a576","module_id":"65f46751-f888-4cef-8899-82a916f8d88f","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:01.094213+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:01.094213+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Submit October review findings","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Check the deck results and prepare an evidence-backed manager update explaining the most relevant variances and unresolved items.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"83d4dc29-e867-487d-9dba-4e71494d7535","module_id":"056822e1-887b-4a10-99e9-70f234cd58b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:06.492663+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:06.492663+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Express: Marketing and Sales Analytics","content":"MODULE 4: Marketing and Sales Analytics\n6E STAGE: Express\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nEXPECTED EXCEL DASHBOARD — MARKETING & SALES\n\nRESOURCE: M4_Marketing_and_Sales_Express.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M4_Express_Acquisition_Sales_Conversion_Diagnostic.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M4_Express_Acquisition_Sales_Conversion_Diagnostic.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1FA6TByldD9R6Bcsp6Cz6SAM954UNNhcU/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"858aad8c-0c8a-4a24-8869-9e87aeca3762","module_id":"42b2abe9-d25a-4686-8887-58a6810cdd28","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:27.474491+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:27.474491+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S21 - Run an Express health API","content":"WHAT: We are starting Grama’s backend and returning a basic health response.\nDO: Install the documented Node/Express dependencies in Grama/server, create the Express server and health endpoint, and start it from the server folder.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The /api/health endpoint answers from localhost:3000.\nIF IT FAILS: Check npm install, the current folder and port 3000 if Express does not start.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 04 PowerPoint, task S21 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S21.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"866ac424-bc62-4f17-92a1-7dd827350ac2","module_id":"8009900c-e018-4848-aab2-f1e19136e26a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:45.161927+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:45.161927+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Grade 11 English — Research Writing, Rhetoric and Communication","content":"Complete Grade 11 English course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"866fd6aa-00b8-4789-a382-21cdd6cc5a99","module_id":"d0afaa26-1b4b-4653-830c-3848d6eaafc5","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:45.307613+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:45.307613+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Draft useful channel-specific copy","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 3 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Use workbook 02_Creative to draft Marketplace and retail messages from verified product facts; keep customer need and next action visible.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"86706db3-573c-45c8-9fab-67c98311e31d","module_id":"7f78ef5d-704e-4360-9363-d268dc2a086e","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:42.021107+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:42.021107+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"T07 - Complete the full five-player form","content":"Work task T07: Complete the full five-player form.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Website & test checkout in the shared offline simulator.\n1. First leave one player name empty and press Submit. See the error.\n2. Fill captain email and all five player names with the shown sample data.\n3. Submit again. Find your TEST registration number.\nCompleted example: Where: Website > Registration form; Team: TEST-GHOST-SQUAD; Captain email: captain@example.com; Five player names: Player One to Player Five; Bad form: Must be rejected.\nCheck in simulator: Must be rejected.\nWhy: A paid team record must contain the player details the organiser needs.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1tJuOwfbw-QCews6r6YS7DyDeJSIcPkOy/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"25","lesson_id":"87cae95f-0f9f-44a5-8b84-71bcc480c7de","module_id":"5ed0a17f-83ab-4746-b1d6-8ab738d6f9eb","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:21.033554+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:21.033554+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Excel Core Foundation — Complete Guided Lesson","content":"Use the attached 116-slide Excel Core Foundation presentation. Follow the 18-step learning loop: Frame (1-4), Locate + Do (5-9), See + Prove (10-13), Recover + Transfer (14-18).\n\nTOPICS:\nE1. Excel Tables & structured references\nE2. Cell references: relative, absolute and mixed\nE3. Core summary functions\nE4. IF, AND, OR and IFERROR\nE5. COUNTIF, SUMIF and AVERAGEIF\nE6. SUMIFS, COUNTIFS and AVERAGEIFS\nE7. XLOOKUP\nE8. FILTER, UNIQUE and SORT\nE9. Text and date preparation\nE10. Business KPIs\nE11. Data tools\nE12. PivotTable\nE13. PivotChart and slicer\nE14. Charts\nE15. Power Query in Excel\nE16. One-page Excel dashboard\nE17. Final independent Excel challenge\n\nPractice workbook named in the slides: Excel_Core_Practice_Workbook_Guided.xlsx (not supplied with the current uploads). The uploaded NovaRetail Data Set.xlsx belongs to the separate MBA analytics lab and is not an exact replacement.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"87d376d2-7cc1-4f8b-b1e4-6a670e1540f8","module_id":"1db3c9d9-1d71-4ce1-a0fc-dac7804e9f40","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:10.912402+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:10.912402+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1}]'::jsonb) r
WHERE r.module_id IN (SELECT module_id FROM public.course_modules WHERE course_id IN (SELECT id FROM lms_demo_missing_courses))
