FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"S02 - Show the first resource","content":"WHAT: We are showing the first verified resource card so residents can locate typing practice.\nDO: Replace the RESOURCE CARDS placeholder in index.html with the initial verified GRC-002 resource card and its visible fields.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Exactly one static resource card appears. Search and filters are still future work.\nIF IT FAILS: Check the cards section and save before refreshing.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 01 PowerPoint, task S02 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S02.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"974f8d90-cf41-46d9-9384-021658981db9","module_id":"94232a37-0467-4fbc-bb04-b11c3a6b98ab","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:33.514088+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:33.514088+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Grade 9 English — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 9 English course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"97a038f9-3754-4e0c-ace2-ec487b2d920d","module_id":"2884de3e-e68e-43a9-ac12-313841a56670","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:25.961173+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:25.961173+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Grade 7 Science — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 7 Science course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"97f5cc63-9f46-4ffc-b8f1-00b727a1488f","module_id":"103a9314-42fb-43cc-80bf-18210d13215e","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:13.421252+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:13.421252+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Grade 12 Computer Science — Data architecture, algorithms and responsible models","content":"Complete Grade 12 Computer Science course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"9817d7f2-648a-46c8-92e9-f76d9da11eca","module_id":"543c55dd-e584-4fd9-90b0-20f7ffffdde2","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:15:11.316035+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:15:11.316035+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Calculate verified Week 2 channel metrics","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 4 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: In 02_Dashboard complete the missing Marketplace and Retail measures; never assign an advertising CTR to retail sampling.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"70","lesson_id":"991817f3-842e-48a4-bf18-b3004ad45aa6","module_id":"2563fa98-58f6-4862-80d8-934090fe4bad","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:45.724055+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:45.724055+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S41 - Verify durable database path","content":"WHAT: We are using a stable SQLite file location so saved records survive restarts.\nDO: Create the DB-path check script, configure durable DB_PATH, submit a fresh pending suggestion, and stop/restart the Node server.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Exactly the same fresh SUG-ID and stable DB_PATH are visible before and after restart.\nIF IT FAILS: CREATE the script first, then check the exact ID; counts alone do not prove persistence.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 07 PowerPoint, task S41 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S41.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"99290ebc-d954-4049-b184-a9f6bdb1fcd7","module_id":"f2a32bfe-3e30-4928-ab08-81ec0f90db87","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:57.405976+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:57.405976+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Contamination and Pollution Fundamentals","content":"Tell a contaminant from a pollutant. Identify physical, chemical and biological contamination. Compare point sources with runoff from many places, then calculate pollutant loading and simple exposure estimates. Read what the evidence supports and what remains unknown.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"9976fd08-3bba-49f2-8a98-b5ed3d0c5746","module_id":"b26cd4c4-63ec-496d-8bb6-9726c7e28499","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:20.565448+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:20.565448+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Update and check the central onboarding tracker","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Carry supported verification results into 02_Onboarding_Tracker, retain unresolved gaps and send only permitted escalations.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"99c2576b-67e1-483d-91e5-cedbc4a1c108","module_id":"a698052a-6425-4f3f-abc5-71ed1fc1f9cf","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:00.999131+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:00.999131+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S19 - Verify the frontend","content":"WHAT: We are checking the website we built before adding the backend.\nDO: Run the frontend checklist for search, filters, mobile layout, drafts, enquiry, backup and offline behavior. Export a final draft backup before changing ports.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The learner records actual PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED results and the original draft ID; grama_drafts_backup.json is downloaded.\nIF IT FAILS: Keep the backup outside Grama/client before Module 04 moves the frontend.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 03 PowerPoint, task S19 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S19.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"99d135e6-6fe3-48cc-9a5c-c6f4e90fd294","module_id":"725cf25c-1179-43c1-92b8-a16610df08b7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:43.737741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:43.737741+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"T14 - Choose who sees the ad","content":"Work task T14: Choose who sees the ad.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ad research in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open the Audience form.\n2. Set Bengaluru, 18 and Local adult gaming teams.\n3. Save the audience brief.\nCompleted example: City: Bengaluru; Minimum age: 18; Audience: Local adult gaming teams.\nCheck in simulator: Local adult gaming teams.\nWhy: Ads should reach people who can really join.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1H-5eW5OhpLbO7DsFnlyXWDHHny8-3LO1/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"99e0c26f-60b9-480b-80f8-78a4aacf9c8e","module_id":"f2f23969-4104-4df2-a4a8-d8687fad4dc6","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:25.28938+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:25.28938+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Calculate store achievement and weak outlets","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 1 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Use workbook 01_Sales to calculate achievement percent and apply the case-specific under-66-percent triage rule to store outlets.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"9a09949e-0d3a-40f3-af62-54e3b1f82e1d","module_id":"29687f58-184a-4af4-a628-043d14f5d175","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:33.518045+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:33.518045+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Read employee and manager Day 30 evidence","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Inspect source checkpoint updates and outstanding issue records, keyed by candidate ID and checkpoint.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"9a453652-e3d3-4c0e-b59e-8c4d05099a74","module_id":"0e53e3e2-0adb-4d30-b8ff-50c1399923f8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:11.795035+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:11.795035+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"T20 - Test starting a payment","content":"Work task T20: Test starting a payment.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Tracking lab in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Press Start checkout.\n2. Find InitiateCheckout in the events list.\n3. Verify no paid team was created yet.\nCompleted example: Test button: Start checkout; Expected event: InitiateCheckout.\nCheck in simulator: InitiateCheckout.\nWhy: Starting to pay is not the same as paying.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1XAIeg9OHnwXONsTjITRLTCOmoFZ4ZXi8/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"9aa2f727-c901-4c7f-b4e7-c26897617c3c","module_id":"8f675f68-d87b-40ab-aeff-7026a8b062ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:28.983725+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:28.983725+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T37 - Run Day 1 and Day 2 only","content":"Work task T37: Run Day 1 and Day 2 only.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Daily ad results in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Daily ad results and load Day 1.\n2. Load Day 2. Read the warning about zero paid teams.\n3. Stop at Day 2 and inspect the funnel.\nCompleted example: Days now available: D1 and D2; Spent: ₹950; Day 2: 85 clicks, zero payments; Next action: Investigate; do not continue.\nCheck in simulator: Investigate; do not continue.\nWhy: You must respond while the campaign is running, not after all six days.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1izzDMQe1LDWcTfFFemfkzLiNafREVXsf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"30","lesson_id":"9ad70992-c61f-4fe2-9ee3-7e097dbdba14","module_id":"9d37547e-5aca-4397-a704-05c09a59cb3a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:39.206822+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:39.206822+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S12 - Add category and empty feedback","content":"WHAT: We are combining category, village and search and showing when no records match.\nDO: Add category filtering, no-match feedback and the final change listener. Save all S12 code first; check search, village and category in combination.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: With other filters cleared, Tools shows two results; wifi returns zero. At 390px the filters fit without horizontal overflow.\nIF IT FAILS: Do not check Category before the event listener is saved; confirm the combined-filter function is complete.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 02 PowerPoint, task S12 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S12.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"9ae068da-4aa2-47d5-9c85-b6814b31dceb","module_id":"7a584fec-8468-485f-aad3-a5fe02e103ca","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:39.471043+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:39.471043+00:00","description":null,"order_index":8},{"title":"Complete Week 4 channel calculations","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 5 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Use 02_Channels to calculate missing Marketplace and retail results. Compare source-specific confirmed events, conversion efficiency and return.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"70","lesson_id":"9be49f80-8fe1-41e4-bdef-c24e52b7089d","module_id":"f555663a-aca5-4d75-b223-634f30c3762b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:49.417246+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:49.417246+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Capture evidence for the final tickets","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Capture only the remaining tickets. Preserve Rohit JOINER evidence saved before his leaver.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 27\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe capture_evidence.py IAM-R-102\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe capture_evidence.py IAM-X-202\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe capture_evidence.py IAM-L-301\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe capture_evidence.py IAM-L-401\nRUN / PERFORM:\nRun after actual tests and real denial screenshots. NEVER recapture IAM-J-201 now.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nEVIDENCE STATUS: PASS_AUTOMATED\nLeavers: PENDING_HUMAN_SCREENSHOT_REVIEW\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nFour ticket files must pass. Preserve original IAM-J-201 proof and its timestamp.\nUNDERSTAND:\nSystem-derived evidence is checked and routed to an IAM reviewer.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 85–86 (Guided task 27). Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"35","lesson_id":"9e966f2f-8983-425b-b0ac-909a2e767c91","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.351168+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.351168+00:00","description":null,"order_index":8},{"title":"Check findings with the guided case","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Compare the conclusion with slide checkpoints and retain failed acceptance conditions for management decision.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"25","lesson_id":"9ea3433d-8c55-4673-9ac9-ab39f37604b0","module_id":"144a0889-2ac7-47f6-8cea-a450a7efd3f1","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:27.862363+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:27.862363+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Prepare the manager review and issue handoff","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Update 07_Issue_Log and 02_Onboarding_Tracker so the manager can see exact unresolved concerns and their owners.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"9eb4da0c-ef60-40ec-8341-49a739b95969","module_id":"1d7fb1bb-786e-440a-8117-c59e29b8dda2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:15.477486+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:15.477486+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Examine stock-age evidence and limitations","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Read pre-calculated stock age and over-120-minute flags, then record evidence notes for affected Jayanagar orders without claiming causation.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"9ef3a6d3-93dc-48ef-b935-ad0b8fd4b665","module_id":"9184ac19-93a3-42ea-90f1-0de8006dab18","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:13.31557+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:13.31557+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Decide what to keep, test, change or pause","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 5 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Complete 03_Decisions after comparing Week 2 and Week 4. Treat unverified event gaps as unresolved rather than making up explanations.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"a0550c09-10d2-4710-8661-1288e7900ab5","module_id":"f555663a-aca5-4d75-b223-634f30c3762b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:50.005067+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:50.005067+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Company Formation - Guided Learning and Practice","content":"Work through Tasks 06-09 with the module learning deck and operating workbook.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"a1604c1d-4806-4066-bf71-c94c38263df4","module_id":"26413b0a-e801-4af2-aa69-b8beaed7d198","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:34.587778+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:37:34.587778+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Give Ananya view-only access","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Add only the approved Finance-Viewers group to the employee account.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 08\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, find_group, group_names, ROOT\ns = connect(\"IAM-J-101\")\nu = find_user(s, \"ananya.shah\")\ng = find_group(s, \"Finance-Viewers\")\nr = s.put(f\"{ROOT}/users/{u[''id'']}/groups/{g[''id'']}\",\n          timeout=15)\nr.raise_for_status()\nprint(\"GROUPS:\", group_names(s, u[\"id\"]))\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nGROUPS: [''Finance-Viewers'']\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nMust include Finance-Viewers.\nMust NOT include Finance-Editors.\nMatch the exact approved group in IAM-J-101.\nUNDERSTAND:\nGroup membership grants the view role to the application.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 37–38 (Guided task 08). Module 03 (Explain).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"a247336e-51ea-41c4-8257-da1dc7af81b5","module_id":"fc3b345d-ea20-4ef5-8693-9796ed1939b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:06.832521+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:06.832521+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Read recruitment handover and updates","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Inspect Source Data 01_Recruitment_Handover and 02_Recruitment_Updates; compare candidate identity, role, team and planned joining date.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"a266fb43-e7d1-4d62-afbb-a9fb02bf0e18","module_id":"fdb51063-72ec-4a25-a5fe-514c4c631648","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:57.294757+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:57.294757+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"T11 - Test booking number 17","content":"Work task T11: Test booking number 17.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Website & test checkout in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Website > Safety tests.\n2. Type 17 in Attempt booking number and run the test.\n3. Read the test log. Team 17 must be blocked.\nCompleted example: Team limit: 16; Attempted next booking: 17; Expected result: BLOCKED — full.\nCheck in simulator: BLOCKED — full.\nWhy: The registration site must not sell more slots than the organiser has.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1tJuOwfbw-QCews6r6YS7DyDeJSIcPkOy/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"a2ecfbd7-1ae5-45f7-b8f3-37e41366dd13","module_id":"5ed0a17f-83ab-4746-b1d6-8ab738d6f9eb","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:23.301242+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:23.301242+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Test the new M-03 code against 11 cases","content":"Execute the 11 supplied transfer test cases on the new M-03 C source. Check expected versus actual states, fix any permitted defect and rerun the full suite. Do not modify the approved transfer CSV to manufacture a PASS. OUTPUT: M-03 11-case test result and generated evidence.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"a3626d98-b8d6-4ed4-bd49-4a0bf51aca4a","module_id":"d09eb39f-3151-4b13-a818-a75a632157f2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:30.951823+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:30.951823+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T47 - Write a report that matches the records","content":"Work task T47: Write a report that matches the records.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Final report in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Final report > Write report.\n2. Fill the four result fields using the verified source records.\n3. Choose the correct status, issue, next action and limitation. Save.\nCompleted example: New paid: 11; Total paid: 16; Spend: ₹2,890; CPA: ₹262.73; Report rule: Every number must match records.\nCheck in simulator: Every number must match records.\nWhy: A long wrong report is still wrong. Every claim needs evidence.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/17IglBQnnnIL9v2w0psRL_Vp2qeuQIzWf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"40","lesson_id":"a3743130-5d85-4af3-bc5d-79b157604bc9","module_id":"216fd3f2-3bed-47da-be6f-5611e637a457","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:45.468331+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:45.468331+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Grade 8 Mathematics — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 8 Mathematics course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"a379fc49-e6b7-4f19-b6e0-c7242a0e204f","module_id":"f73d7639-6df3-4c21-9eb4-9b9db2fa32ed","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:17.607888+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:17.607888+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Prepare the initial channel budget","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 3 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: In workbook 01_Budget calculate and verify the four-channel Rs 1,20,000 plan and the role of each channel.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"a38ac558-2fa6-4f60-b928-f325a0aedcbc","module_id":"7f78ef5d-704e-4360-9363-d268dc2a086e","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:41.452533+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:41.452533+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T45 - Match the final numbers","content":"Work task T45: Match the final numbers.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Final report in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Final report > Reconcile.\n2. Enter spend and total paid bookings.\n3. Press Verify totals.\nCompleted example: Campaign spend: ₹2,890; New paid: 11; Total paid: 16.\nCheck in simulator: 16.\nWhy: The ad report and actual team records must agree.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/17IglBQnnnIL9v2w0psRL_Vp2qeuQIzWf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"25","lesson_id":"a47151be-6196-48b7-8bdf-638f84c2d187","module_id":"216fd3f2-3bed-47da-be6f-5611e637a457","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:44.328711+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:44.328711+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Installing Python","content":"Download and install Python on your computer...","duration":"20 minutes","lesson_id":"a521682b-277e-4534-a8a3-d62b6cf0593f","module_id":"f1f25064-999a-4fd3-8d6c-03eeb8db8f29","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:07:50.409234+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T06:07:50.409234+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Boss Challenge: Repair and Create","content":"In the simulator, find and repair the incorrect coin. Build a new repeating unit with three lane positions that is not a copy or rotation of the taught pattern. Predict position 17 and show the mathematical rule.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"a737bc9a-5841-4b6b-afe6-84b10ac47ff5","module_id":"d761eb0b-f00c-4dd6-9f36-b7f2f65f8f65","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:49.918818+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:49.918818+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Start the identity system","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Start Keycloak. This is where employee accounts and access groups are stored.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\ndocker compose up -d\ndocker compose ps  (shared setup, before .venv exists)\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\ndocker compose up -d\ndocker compose ps\nRUN / PERFORM:\nPowerShell: execute both lines in iam_l1_lab.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\niam-l1-keycloak | running\n(Exact Docker wording may vary.)\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin/\nKeycloak login page must appear.\nIf not, inspect: docker compose logs keycloak\nUNDERSTAND:\nThe identity system must be running before we can change access.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 20–21 (Guided task 01). Module 02 (Explore).","duration":"75","lesson_id":"a7fc9435-abd5-4961-a2ee-4d24d2a2f70b","module_id":"11649aa6-8081-45b1-bd24-94c42727b4dd","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:03.663477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:03.663477+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"S24 - Seed eight resources only once","content":"WHAT: We are loading the eight existing Grama records into SQLite without duplicates.\nDO: Create the seed script and load the eight verified Grama resources into SQLite. Run seeding twice.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: First seed inserts eight records; the second inserts zero duplicates.\nIF IT FAILS: Confirm unique IDs and the right DB_PATH if counts differ.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 04 PowerPoint, task S24 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S24.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"a870f8db-40b3-4b85-a692-67c07baf492d","module_id":"8009900c-e018-4848-aab2-f1e19136e26a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:46.867939+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:46.867939+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Track open issues and approved probation decisions","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete 14_Transfer_Issues and 15_Transfer_Probation, documenting owner, evidence, manager approval and closure state.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"65","lesson_id":"a8a6689a-eaca-464e-b362-c47bb8b19678","module_id":"1a9397ae-439a-4b11-a6a7-a53ccaa97535","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:22.292834+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:22.292834+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"T24 - Reject duplicate Purchase and reconcile","content":"Work task T24: Reject duplicate Purchase and reconcile.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Tracking lab in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open the Purchase event list and find the repeated event.\n2. Mark the repeated event EXCLUDED in the REPORT (you do not edit production tracking).\n3. Raise a tracking-owner ticket. Verify one valid Purchase for one captured payment.\nCompleted example: Booking: CA-TEST-001; Captured payment: TX-TEST-001; Accepted Purchase: Exactly one; Repeated event: REJECTED.\nCheck in simulator: REJECTED.\nWhy: A repeated tracking signal must not be counted as another paid booking.\nYour role: exclude a repeated Purchase from the training report and notify the tracking owner; do not change live tracking code.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1XAIeg9OHnwXONsTjITRLTCOmoFZ4ZXi8/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"35","lesson_id":"a8da9380-ad8d-494d-b5d2-d911b06bda1f","module_id":"8f675f68-d87b-40ab-aeff-7026a8b062ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:31.25839+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:31.25839+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7}]'::jsonb) r
WHERE r.module_id IN (SELECT module_id FROM public.course_modules WHERE course_id IN (SELECT id FROM lms_demo_missing_courses))
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

SELECT r."title", r."content", r."duration", r."lesson_id", r."module_id", r."created_at", r."updated_at", r."description", r."order_index"
FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"S43 - Smoke test and hand over Grama","content":"WHAT: We are checking the real hosted app and recording truthful release evidence.\nDO: On an approved HTTPS host only, configure SITE_URL and persistent storage, run the smoke test, and verify a record after service restart.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Report real HTTPS/health/data/persistence evidence; if no approved host is supplied, report BLOCKED.\nIF IT FAILS: Do not enter a fabricated host URL or infer deployment success from localhost.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 07 PowerPoint, task S43 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S43.","duration":"75","lesson_id":"a8ea1237-48f6-48c4-913d-03e163ea66ba","module_id":"f2a32bfe-3e30-4928-ab08-81ec0f90db87","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:58.540299+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:58.540299+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Receive the thirty-day follow-up assignment","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Identify what Day 30 checks can confirm, what remains unverified, and which manager decisions are outside HR coordinator authority.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"a937d52b-79d4-4ff6-94d4-43345b0047b9","module_id":"0e53e3e2-0adb-4d30-b8ff-50c1399923f8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:11.229151+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:11.229151+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Check closure against unresolved issues","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Update the main 02_Onboarding_Tracker and 07_Issue_Log only where source evidence permits closure; preserve extensions and blockers.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"a9902578-f52f-4a7a-bf5b-889200af39dd","module_id":"77df4865-88d1-4fb4-9b03-948bf7a87499","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:18.026611+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:18.026611+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Evaluate options within the supplied constraints","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete M4_TO_BE_DESIGN!C15:G17, compare trade-offs and justify the preferred process direction.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"aace54b9-bc2b-4b58-a30c-82ff69503a2e","module_id":"4ebcf693-3bd3-4361-805c-aab771f99ee8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:21.046313+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:21.046313+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"T17 - Export four real creative image files","content":"Work task T17: Export four real creative image files.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ad creative studio in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Feed and Reel for Ad A, then Ad B.\n2. Press Check claims. Export the four PNG images.\n3. Check that text does not overlap the Register button. The simulator must reject any text that cannot fit.\nCompleted example: Ad A: Feed 4:5 and Reel 9:16; Ad B: Feed 4:5 and Reel 9:16; Deliverable: Four PNG files in one ZIP.\nCheck in simulator: Four PNG files in one ZIP.\nWhy: A phone preview alone is not an ad asset. We must give the manager the four image files.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1H-5eW5OhpLbO7DsFnlyXWDHHny8-3LO1/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"50","lesson_id":"ab596233-bc0b-4fae-b4fe-b713f186ef40","module_id":"f2f23969-4104-4df2-a4a8-d8687fad4dc6","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:26.988927+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:26.988927+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Grant only Rohit’s approved group","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Add Finance-Viewers only, then inspect the saved membership.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 18\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, find_group, group_names, ROOT\ns = connect(\"IAM-J-201\")\nu = find_user(s, \"rohit.nair\")\ng = find_group(s, \"Finance-Viewers\")\nr = s.put(f\"{ROOT}/users/{u[''id'']}/groups/{g[''id'']}\",\n          timeout=15)\nr.raise_for_status()\nprint(\"GROUPS:\", group_names(s, u[\"id\"]))\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nGROUPS: [''Finance-Viewers'']\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nFinance-Viewers present.\nFinance-Editors absent.\nThe role must match IAM-J-201 exactly.\nUNDERSTAND:\nThe same workflow can serve another person without increasing privileges.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 62–63 (Guided task 18). Module 05 (Empower).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"abc1d218-f8d9-45d3-9b01-1ee996d03d92","module_id":"6d083266-9280-4761-a335-079183e1eb66","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:11.373697+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:11.373697+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"S36 - Implement login and sessions","content":"WHAT: We are authenticating coordinators with sessions and protecting review routes.\nDO: Implement coordinator login, cookie-backed sessions and route protection in Express.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: An authenticated coordinator can reach review routes; an anonymous visitor cannot.\nIF IT FAILS: Restart server after route edits and verify login/session responses with complete PowerShell commands.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 06 PowerPoint, task S36 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S36.","duration":"75","lesson_id":"add6e0fc-70d0-4b66-884a-d39f61bbfdb7","module_id":"700759e6-a8d5-4d9f-9c79-6e724f3c101a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:54.272065+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:54.272065+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"T41 - Write an evidence-based Day 2 finding","content":"Work task T41: Write an evidence-based Day 2 finding.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Daily ad results in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Day 2 records. Inspect failed and abandoned payment entries.\n2. Choose Hold the budget while checking. Do not spend more until the fault is understood.\n3. Mark the suspected cause and note F-010 and F-011, then save.\nCompleted example: Day 2 clicks: 85; Forms: 14; Checkout starts: 4; Paid teams: 0; Evidence: F-010 and F-011 failed.\nCheck in simulator: F-010 and F-011 failed.\nWhy: Zero payments is an anomaly. Payment logs support a hypothesis, not yet a proven cause.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1p5dgB1Wh8E_nYr3b2sRuFnGUaDykfjci/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"35","lesson_id":"ae2ad539-a951-4807-b139-46b13ba6b08a","module_id":"03d4e523-70dc-43cb-bb14-d1028f8d3f49","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:41.757042+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:41.757042+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Complete conditional transfer and handover","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Finish 07_TRANSFER with the hypothetical effect only if approved and posted. Submit the manager review and unresolved evidence log for authorized review.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"af08d244-53de-4a25-9b5c-32cfa3ac0703","module_id":"d61fd402-a087-41e8-bb8c-b4021a36f869","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:09.617069+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:09.617069+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Decide what to do with a pending credit note","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Evaluate supplemental credit note TRANSFER-CN-01 for Rs 2,000. Record the missing approval/posting and the correct L1 action in TRANSFER_EVIDENCE!B10:B11; do not post.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"afbb133f-6585-415c-851a-d22738b7d3e3","module_id":"d61fd402-a087-41e8-bb8c-b4021a36f869","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:09.048996+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:09.048996+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Evolve: Business Analytics","content":"MODULE 2: Business Analytics\n6E STAGE: Evolve\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nBUILD THE BUSINESS ANALYTICS POWER BI DASHBOARD\nLoad BA_Order and BA_Process.\nUse Month and Region dimensions.\nCreate Orders, AOV, Delivery Days, Return Rate, Complaint Rate, Satisfaction and Delay measures.\nAdd KPI cards.\nAdd Delivery by Region, Return / Complaint trend and Delay by Stage.\nAdd Month, Region and Sales Channel slicers.\n\nRESOURCE: M2_Business_Analytics_Evolve.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M2_Evolve_Process_Bottleneck_Action_Brief.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M2_Evolve_Process_Bottleneck_Action_Brief.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Gv1I6il3p-UEp1yX1ATx1Eii3folMFXq/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"afeb38c4-2a76-4e6e-9052-c8d3ceb29129","module_id":"56bcb15d-8908-460a-9eb0-e8fe9461a59c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:21.185447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:21.185447+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Test Ananya in the real portal","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Prove that the new employee can view reports but cannot edit them.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 10\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nStart-Process \"http://127.0.0.1:5000/?ticket=IAM-J-101\"\nRUN / PERFORM:\nPowerShell: open portal and perform BOTH click tests.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nSIGNED IN: ananya.shah\nView report -> 200 | Report visible\nEdit report -> 403 | Access denied\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nUse a NEW private browser window on reference portal :5001.\nSign in: ananya.shah / AnanyaLab!2026.\nCheck displayed username.\nView must PASS; edit must be DENIED.\nUNDERSTAND:\nTwo tests are necessary: permission granted and excessive privilege blocked.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 41–42 (Guided task 10). Module 03 (Explain).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"b07ad970-b75a-4103-a9ed-9fbbccb9094e","module_id":"fc3b345d-ea20-4ef5-8693-9796ed1939b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:07.401098+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:07.401098+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"Record and check cash priorities","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Compare module expected results and write a finance-manager follow-up with verified overdue and excess-stock figures, owner and evidence gaps.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"b34d0b04-bdb0-4b38-a59a-85156abd33f0","module_id":"c02814cb-fc5f-4e0c-8756-451d7d0843a4","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:59.667841+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:59.667841+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Observe Mira’s denial and verify repair authority","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Find the cause of Mira Khan’s denied report view before changing her permissions.\n1. Visit http://127.0.0.1:5000/?ticket=IAM-R-102 in a new private browser session and test View. Observe HTTP 403 BEFORE the repair.\n2. Find the existing mira.khan identity and current groups. Compare actual membership with the approved Finance-Viewers entitlement.\n3. Only after the evidence comparison run: .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe approval_check.py IAM-R-102\nCHECK: User exists and can sign in; Finance-Viewers is missing; IAM-R-102 permits only the approved repair.\nUNDERSTAND: A successful login does not prove the employee has report-view permission. Never create a duplicate Mira account to fix membership.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 46–47. Module 04 (Express).","duration":"25","lesson_id":"b35b1620-acf3-4576-bb71-37d94f4904fe","module_id":"9226bb2b-cd3e-4f73-82c1-66c0e5320bd7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:08.252159+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:08.252159+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Write and verify the evidence-based problem finding","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Complete M1_ANALYSIS!B65 with the strongest observed pattern, scope, and unresolved cause; check the result against the guided deck.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"b3ccb3f1-9cd6-4ad6-bb85-23667aa01aed","module_id":"9184ac19-93a3-42ea-90f1-0de8006dab18","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:13.88388+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:13.88388+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Log a Whitefield field-execution issue","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Open the complete self-paced ZIP; Module 4 presentation, source and learner workbook are inside its 01_Learner_Modules folder.\nDO: Record late sampling, responsible owner, current status, follow-up and review date in workbook 01_Execution.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"b3fc224b-8ab6-460e-a147-c911169b76d8","module_id":"2563fa98-58f6-4862-80d8-934090fe4bad","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:45.147947+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:45.147947+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Independent assessment — Neha’s leaver and evidence handover","content":"WORKPLACE MISSION: Process Neha Iyer’s NEW authorized leaver ticket IAM-L-502 after her independent IAM-J-501 joiner is completed.\n1. Verify the leaver approval and exact identity.\n2. Remove only the approved Finance-Viewers group.\n3. Disable neha.iyer, then test a fresh login and confirm it is rejected.\n4. Capture a separate IAM-L-502 leaver evidence file. Do not replace the earlier IAM-J-501 joiner proof.\n5. RUN: .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe handover.py assessment\nEXPECTED RESULT: Neha is disabled, has no viewer group, the saved joiner proof remains intact, and assessment evidence reaches IAM-ASSESSMENT-REVIEW for pending human review.\nUNDERSTAND: No completed solution code is supplied in this assessment. A supervisor must accept the work evidence.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 88. Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"90","lesson_id":"b79e75a8-fd82-43c4-849f-de30085f9d44","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.919805+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.919805+00:00","description":null,"order_index":10},{"title":"Understand the sixty-day manager review","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Read the boundary between recording observed performance support needs and making a probation decision.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"b8afe66f-bc1f-4f2d-8580-5b4ecbd757d8","module_id":"1d7fb1bb-786e-440a-8117-c59e29b8dda2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:13.778396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:13.778396+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Module 06 - Human Breathing and Diaphragm","content":"Follow the approved BODY QUEST slides 62-81 (20 slides). Pause to attempt every question in writing before checking the answer, use feedback, and retry where requested.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"b8cac3a3-7245-49a0-ac4d-b2c687c9abbd","module_id":"94517387-4902-4e58-8bbf-861697f94d07","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:59.013029+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:59.013029+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Understand the Day 7 check-in and issue workflow","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Read why candidate concerns need explicit source, assigned owner, next action and status rather than an untracked promise.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"b90b5f4e-3683-471c-9adf-b7e3c4607c0e","module_id":"fd462bb9-9a77-4355-ac64-2859a808c0f2","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:08.113761+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:08.113761+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Inspect receivables and inventory evidence","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Open SEP_RECEIVABLES and SEP_INVENTORY in the source file. Check due dates, report dates, quantities, costs and the unit used.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"b95fcb1d-bc73-47a3-b7fe-722261a5c118","module_id":"c02814cb-fc5f-4e0c-8756-451d7d0843a4","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:57.969918+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:57.969918+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Explore: Finance Analytics","content":"MODULE 1: Finance Analytics\n6E STAGE: Explore\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nFINANCE EXCEL FORMULAS\nREVENUE VARIANCE\nRevenue_Actual_INR - Revenue_Budget_INR\nREVENUE VARIANCE %\nRevenue Variance / Revenue_Budget_INR\nOPERATING PROFIT\nRevenue_Actual_INR - COGS_Actual_INR -\nPayroll_Actual_INR - Marketing_Actual_INR -\nOther_Opex_Actual_INR\nOPERATING MARGIN %\nOperating Profit / Revenue_Actual_INR\nDSO\nReceivables_Closing_INR /\nCredit_Sales_INR * 30\nINVENTORY DAYS\nInventory_Closing_INR /\nCredit_Purchases_INR * 30\nDPO\nPayables_Closing_INR /\nCredit_Purchases_INR * 30\nCASH CONVERSION CYCLE\nDSO + Inventory Days - DPO\nCreate PivotTables by Period and Region.\n\nRESOURCE: M1_Finance_Explore.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"b9d26b07-9f9b-410d-9026-9dfab0cf29f3","module_id":"a4e8da2a-aba5-4f08-b27c-c417f244968c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:16.19139+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:16.19139+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Your first day as a graduate embedded engineer","content":"Workplace: the fictional Peenya electronics lab. Customer: ShreePack Packaging. Your assigned equipment is conveyor Motor M-02. Your L1 job is to test an existing controller warning and document results; you do not certify machinery or release production code. OUTPUT: name your role, motor and assigned engineering change.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"ba1a6591-03b6-4c56-9262-a624ccea4d53","module_id":"e05a5029-3776-445a-bdf7-209387c8eb3c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:22.712214+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:22.712214+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Express: Course Setup and Lab Readiness","content":"MODULE 0: Course Setup and Lab Readiness\n6E STAGE: Express\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nEXCEL WORKFLOW\nTable → Clean → Calculate → Pivot → Chart → Interpret\n\nRESOURCE: M0_Course_Setup_Express.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M0_Express_Lab_Readiness_Data-Quality_Plan.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M0_Express_Lab_Readiness_Data-Quality_Plan.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dty3nRswAQB7UTjgRO61-hzmljrTYHwL/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"bad20341-d8eb-4a5f-9070-0836bf0e09ff","module_id":"cf79daa7-c6cd-45ae-b28c-77635b6e983b","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:13.820122+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:13.820122+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Evolve: HR Analytics","content":"MODULE 3: HR Analytics\n6E STAGE: Evolve\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nBUILD THE HR POWER BI DASHBOARD\nLoad workforce, recruitment and onboarding; use Month / Period, Region and Role dimensions.\nCreate Exit Rate, OT/Employee, Engagement, Vacancies, Applications, Offer Acceptance and Joining Rate measures.\nAdd trend, regional comparison and recruitment funnel visuals.\nAdd Region / Period slicers.\n\nRESOURCE: M3_HR_Evolve.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M3_Evolve_HR_Capacity_Retention_Action_Brief.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M3_Evolve_HR_Capacity_Retention_Action_Brief.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1KWoOD9KRHRGQWZjDg-3VwSIYFifIAAJS/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"bd668e0a-f9e9-46d3-b34b-035b935cc412","module_id":"8759a2fe-d783-4917-9716-d5383a2387ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:24.572544+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:24.572544+00:00","description":null,"order_index":5},{"title":"Capture actual access evidence","content":"PREREQUISITE: In a NEW private window, visit http://127.0.0.1:5000/?ticket=IAM-J-101 and observe real View HTTP 200 and Edit HTTP 403 events. Capture the evidence before any Ananya offboarding operation.\n\nWHAT WE ARE DOING: Read Ananya''s ticket proof from saved Keycloak state and the actual Report Portal event log.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 11\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe capture_evidence.py IAM-J-101\nRUN / PERFORM:\nRun in the lab folder after BOTH browser actions; then open evidence/IAM-J-101.json.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nEVIDENCE STATUS: PASS_AUTOMATED\nFILE: evidence/IAM-J-101.json\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nViewer-only state and real View 200 / Edit 403 events required. If INCOMPLETE, retest; never type PASS.\nUNDERSTAND:\nThe checker uses real Keycloak state and portal events, not typed answers.\nNEXT STEP / EVIDENCE:\nPreserve evidence/IAM-J-101.json for Module 06; do not overwrite the joiner proof.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 44–45 (Guided task 11). Module 03 (Explain).","duration":"40","lesson_id":"bd875284-ca4e-457c-9b7e-f0bd9c91558c","module_id":"fc3b345d-ea20-4ef5-8693-9796ed1939b5","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:07.680988+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:07.680988+00:00","description":null,"order_index":8},{"title":"Open the current-process task and source cards","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Use the guided deck to understand the AS-IS portfolio and examine six process source cards P1-P6.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"be767dbf-d3be-4a9d-a199-7a2cc4850de8","module_id":"00a3db8f-40b2-4d86-9c83-62c4bcc12ef3","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:14.734581+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:14.734581+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Sequence and map the AS-IS process","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Sequence P1-P6 and complete M2_AS_IS_MAP!A16:D21 using the source-to-action path; compare the flow only after attempting.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"be8f4fba-90ef-4477-8311-83f43ad71603","module_id":"00a3db8f-40b2-4d86-9c83-62c4bcc12ef3","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:15.881794+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:15.881794+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"S13 - Build the suggestion form","content":"WHAT: We are collecting six fields for a local resource suggestion.\nDO: Build the visitor suggestion form in index.html with title, category, village, place, hours and source fields. Apply the shown field limits.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Six labelled fields are available; visitors cannot set the record ID or verification status.\nIF IT FAILS: Check each input name and maxlength against the field map.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 03 PowerPoint, task S13 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S13.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"befb96c5-2972-4bec-b5fc-661e2be722c7","module_id":"725cf25c-1179-43c1-92b8-a16610df08b7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:40.323963+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:40.323963+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Grade 10 Chemistry — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 10 Chemistry course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"bfa1df95-1a74-475a-94a9-400c0f9ffd56","module_id":"2b788b64-9c6f-44d9-99ba-b0ade636ea63","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:35.689751+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:35.689751+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T13 - Study three training example ads","content":"Work task T13: Study three training example ads.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ad research in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Open Ad research. Read the three labelled FICTIONAL ad cards.\n2. Tick two ads. In your note, name the exact call-to-action seen in both.\n3. Confirm these are training examples, then Save research. Real ads need outside verification.\nCompleted example: Tool: Meta Ad Library (needs internet); Evidence: Three different ad links; Record: Visible offer and CTA.\nCheck in simulator: Visible offer and CTA.\nWhy: Practice noticing what an advertisement really says. Fictional examples are not competitor evidence.\nThe offline ad examples are fictional. Real competitor evidence requires internet verification.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1H-5eW5OhpLbO7DsFnlyXWDHHny8-3LO1/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"c23fac0c-a75d-47c5-be26-c0147d1167ac","module_id":"f2f23969-4104-4df2-a4a8-d8687fad4dc6","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:24.719892+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:24.719892+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"General Chemistry for Water Engineers","content":"Understand atoms, ions and dissolved solutions. Read the pH scale, explain acids, bases and buffering, and calculate alkalinity from a titration example. Use a balanced chemical equation to identify the limiting reagent and solve a new chemical problem.","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"c2575a59-b945-4620-8aa2-7d082a3f010f","module_id":"10457169-325b-42b1-bd11-635715b74fa6","created_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:26.536454+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-17T06:34:26.536454+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1}]'::jsonb) r
