SELECT r."title", r."content", r."duration", r."lesson_id", r."module_id", r."created_at", r."updated_at", r."description", r."order_index"
FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public."lessons", '[{"title":"Run the final state regression check","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Prove Mira remains fixed while Ananya and Rohit remain disabled.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 26\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe check_state.py repair-provision\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe check_state.py guided-revoke\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe check_state.py independent-revoke\nRUN / PERFORM:\nPowerShell: run all three commands, then finish evidence.\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nEach command prints STAGE, USER, individual PASS lines and a final message.\nThe next slides show the literal output.\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nSave the actual multi-command transcript. Confirm Mira view=200/edit=403 and fresh-login denial proof for Ananya and Rohit.\nUNDERSTAND:\nA lifecycle check looks at the current state of every relevant account.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 83–84 (Guided task 26). Module 06 (Evolve).","duration":"45","lesson_id":"ea8b02c7-6ba5-465f-b7a3-b9e5cd1411b8","module_id":"08ce89f2-829a-4f61-8004-4bb83c2c6ff7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.06649+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:15.06649+00:00","description":null,"order_index":7},{"title":"Discover the hidden rule and the Maths name","content":"Watch the two classroom scoreboards. Subtract neighbouring scores and decide which row changes equally. Discover the mathematical name Arithmetic Progression before moving to first term, common difference and independent practice.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"eab879de-7374-4570-bc70-9a01149da975","module_id":"307d06a3-fea2-4ab1-8c05-797ce3df083c","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:54.062855+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:54.062855+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"S06 - Make search work","content":"WHAT: We are making the search field hide cards that do not match the typed text.\nDO: In app.js, add the search input listener to show and hide cards using typed text.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: Typing wifi gives zero matching cards; typing typing shows the first resource.\nIF IT FAILS: Check the input ID, event listener and Chrome Console.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 02 PowerPoint, task S06 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S06.","duration":"40","lesson_id":"ead55544-e6d0-4465-a620-f82751495161","module_id":"7a584fec-8468-485f-aad3-a5fe02e103ca","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:36.068784+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:36.068784+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Create Rohit from the approved ticket","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Use the new approved employee details to create exactly one Rohit account.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 16\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, ROOT\ns = connect(\"IAM-J-201\")\nassert find_user(s, \"rohit.nair\") is None, \"HOLD: duplicate\"\nrecord = {\n    \"username\": \"rohit.nair\", \"firstName\": \"Rohit\",\n    \"lastName\": \"Nair\", \"email\": \"rohit.nair@example.test\",\n    \"enabled\": True\n}\nr = s.post(f\"{ROOT}/users\", json=record, timeout=15)\nr.raise_for_status()\nu = find_user(s, \"rohit.nair\")\nprint(\"CREATED:\", u[\"username\"], \"| ENABLED:\", u[\"enabled\"])\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nCREATED: rohit.nair | ENABLED: True\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nKeycloak has ONE matching Rohit identity.\nName and email must match IAM-J-201.\nDo not copy Ananya''s identity data.\nUNDERSTAND:\nThe second account demonstrates that you can repeat the real operation.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 58–59 (Guided task 16). Module 05 (Empower).","duration":"60","lesson_id":"eb2f9a7e-b23f-4b69-929f-8c41623a1440","module_id":"6d083266-9280-4761-a335-079183e1eb66","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:10.805387+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:10.805387+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Skill Ecosystem Orientation — Discover, Explore, Demonstrate, Navigate","content":"PARTICIPANT INTRODUCTION: Skill Ecosystem Orientation\nDiscover your strengths, develop capabilities and demonstrate your progress.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL EXPLORE\n1. Discover — Understand how interests, strengths and assessments inform your starting point.\n2. Explore — See how skills, career roles and learning pathways are connected.\n3. Demonstrate — Learn how projects and work samples build your portfolio and Skill Passport.\n4. Navigate — Identify your next activity and how to follow your learning progress.\n\nSESSION FOCUS: Connect self-discovery, skill development and evidence of capability.\n\nRESOURCE: See the attached Skill Ecosystem Orientation introductory presentation.","duration":"","lesson_id":"ec554bc1-b2cc-4924-a11d-e4043c3c8d8d","module_id":"ad1d9a58-c453-45e3-8b9b-7d457d79b395","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:45:32.418223+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-10T06:36:36.583114+00:00","description":"","order_index":1},{"title":"Read the role-based setup request","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Identify required access, equipment, workplace facility and dependency owners without granting system access as an HR analyst.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"edd50590-65f3-40c0-9f86-1860a726ae29","module_id":"067167c1-86b5-4777-b5a0-a4df453dd68c","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:01.851124+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:01.851124+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Read the launch sales and customer evidence","content":"WORKPLACE: SwaadFit Foods and GrainGlow Foods - fictional packaged snacks marketing cases. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Read the unchanged SwaadFit_M1_Source.xlsx records for 12 store outlets, online sales, 214 customer responses, competitor offers and stock availability.\n CHECK: Save the working record; open 90_Check_After_Attempt only after completing the task; do not invent approval, actual spending, conversion events or causal claims.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"ee095b3f-3c05-4be3-b71f-714d6b56a10c","module_id":"29687f58-184a-4af4-a628-043d14f5d175","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:32.95149+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:32.95149+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Explore the Two Signals (optional presentation)","content":"Observe the number and polygon sequences. Make a prediction before the solution slides, then use the counter and polygon demonstrations to understand the rules.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"ee46f646-0103-417a-87c4-4c880d828c0f","module_id":"7c78ebee-8cbe-4c88-9b17-7dcdd312ccc4","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:47.099858+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:47.099858+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Explain: Marketing and Sales Analytics","content":"MODULE 4: Marketing and Sales Analytics\n6E STAGE: Explain\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nMARKETING & SALES — ANSWER CHECK\nSouth\nSouth shows weaker marketing efficiency and much weaker sales conversion in Jul–Sep.\n\nRESOURCE: M4_Marketing_and_Sales_Explain.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"ef2458c0-adbc-454d-9736-9aca6057862f","module_id":"42b2abe9-d25a-4686-8887-58a6810cdd28","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:26.948246+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:26.948246+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"S03 - Style the Grama page","content":"WHAT: We are making the page and resource card readable rather than leaving browser defaults.\nDO: Apply the Grama page and card styles in styles.css: spacing, colors, type, hero area and readable resource card.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The page visibly changes from browser defaults to a styled directory.\nIF IT FAILS: Check the CSS filename and refresh the open page.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 01 PowerPoint, task S03 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S03.","duration":"45","lesson_id":"f0bce372-6b1d-46fa-ab85-b9d67b0fad42","module_id":"94232a37-0467-4fbc-bb04-b11c3a6b98ab","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:34.080203+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:34.080203+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"Understand stakeholder inputs and BA scope","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Read the task and worked example converting one stakeholder statement into a requirement and measurable check.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"f0eed0b4-c480-4d70-aa40-14db71c486de","module_id":"239ff18f-a7a8-4b28-b422-9dca596c667d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:17.299887+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:17.299887+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Grade 6 Mathematics — River Water","content":"Complete Grade 6 Mathematics course presentation. Open the linked PowerPoint in resource_url for the full teaching content, examples and activities.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"f216b9df-29a2-445f-ad15-a844552bc747","module_id":"3034c593-f095-4f09-b9d8-e5932d94f955","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:03.712485+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T09:14:03.712485+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Classify and rewrite testable requirements","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Complete classifications and requirement statements in M3_REQUIREMENTS!D12:E18, including Needs clarification for missing thresholds.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"f2e217d0-10f5-412e-bac4-33fdfed5b2ce","module_id":"239ff18f-a7a8-4b28-b422-9dca596c667d","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:18.436279+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:18.436279+00:00","description":null,"order_index":3},{"title":"What is Python?","content":"Python is a high-level programming language...","duration":"30 minutes","lesson_id":"f675bf78-59c3-47f6-91a1-588e4e67d806","module_id":"f1f25064-999a-4fd3-8d6c-03eeb8db8f29","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:07:49.330691+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T06:07:49.330691+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Start the independent employee transfer case","content":"WORKPLACE: Aarohan Auto Components - fictional employee onboarding simulation. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Open the new batch work order and understand that TR-201 to TR-203 have no worked answer row in the learner workbook.\n CHECK: Verify candidate ID, evidence, status and responsible owner. Do not mark pending items complete.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"f73e375f-f509-4169-940c-478b8bcab4d7","module_id":"1a9397ae-439a-4b11-a6a7-a53ccaa97535","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:19.456623+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:51:19.456623+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Calculate excess inventory exposure","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Record answers in the linked learner workbook. Use the same module source and guided deck from Drive.\nDO: Use 04_STOCK to estimate stock days and value above the 12-day target; distinguish valuation from cash received.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"55","lesson_id":"f74f575b-2d9b-4458-bb7a-163ecf109c99","module_id":"c02814cb-fc5f-4e0c-8756-451d7d0843a4","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:59.106536+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:59.106536+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Locate Mira’s access failure","content":"WHAT WE ARE DOING: Mira can log in but cannot view a report. Find the existing account and missing group.\nI SHOW — REFERENCE: Observe the paired reference action in the separate reference environment.\nREFERENCE ACTION / COMMAND:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe reference_show.py 12\n# REFERENCE realm only; do NOT run work.py yet.\nI TRY — EXACT REPEAT: Use the same code or clicks shown, unchanged, in your own learner lab. For Python tasks, put the complete code below into the learner work.py file. Do not repeat a state-changing account creation twice in the same realm.\nCODE / EXACT TOOL ACTION:\nfrom iam_api import connect, find_user, group_names\ns = connect()\nu = find_user(s, \"mira.khan\")\nassert u, \"STOP: existing account missing\"\nprint(\"BEFORE:\", u[\"username\"])\nprint(\"GROUPS:\", group_names(s, u[\"id\"]))\nRUN / PERFORM:\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe work.py\nEXPECTED RESULT:\nBEFORE: mira.khan\nGROUPS: []\nPortal view (before fix): 403\nCHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:\nNew private login: mira.khan / MiraLab!2026.\nCheck View report = 403 BEFORE the fix.\nDo not create a duplicate identity.\nUNDERSTAND:\nSuccessful login does not mean the user has the requested permission.\n\nSOURCE: Approved IAM L1 v8, source slide(s) 48–49 (Guided task 12). Module 04 (Express).","duration":"35","lesson_id":"f9c65f36-843d-458a-93f8-15324b64ab03","module_id":"9226bb2b-cd3e-4f73-82c1-66c0e5320bd7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:08.819093+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:08.819093+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Inspect budget, P&L and product-cost records","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Compare SEP_BUDGET, SEP_PNL_ACTUAL, SEP_PRODUCT_PLAN, SEP_PRODUCT_ACTUAL and SEP_COST_DETAIL, keeping planned and realised costs separate.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"f9f5c31a-c25a-4e34-bd47-6dfa6021744e","module_id":"5d6e6c3b-27f1-4069-9272-fb255d0feb98","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:54.861165+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:54.861165+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Check the forecast and proposed actions","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Compare checked forecast and action outputs against the deck, record uncertainty and prepare decision notes for Finance Manager review.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"30","lesson_id":"fa1870a1-3860-4d2d-b0d0-ea581b99729f","module_id":"65f46751-f888-4cef-8899-82a916f8d88f","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:03.37134+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:03.37134+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"S20 - Add a backend to the same Grama","content":"WHAT: We are moving our finished website into client/ and creating an Express server folder.\nDO: Create client/ and server/ within the SAME Grama project; move the five completed frontend files into client/ and prepare the Express directory.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The five frontend files are in Grama/client and the backend folder exists; the JSON backup is kept separately.\nIF IT FAILS: Create destination directories BEFORE moving files, and stop using the frontend-only launcher after S20.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 04 PowerPoint, task S20 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S20.","duration":"60","lesson_id":"fab11855-3cc9-476f-8b92-c1485bb610f0","module_id":"8009900c-e018-4848-aab2-f1e19136e26a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:44.595828+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:44.595828+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Module 08 - Animal Breathing and the Final Mission","content":"Follow the approved BODY QUEST slides 103-138 (36 slides). Pause to attempt every question in writing before checking the answer, use feedback, and retry where requested.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"fac9717d-affa-4ea0-876c-ba7b042b1626","module_id":"a0d2100c-dedd-4179-b425-3b653674345e","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:48:00.060021+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:48:00.060021+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"T09 - Try a failed test payment","content":"Work task T09: Try a failed test payment.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Website & test checkout in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Press Create another test form.\n2. Choose Fail: test payment.\n3. Check that the team is not confirmed.\nCompleted example: Method: Failed test; Payment: failed; Booking: not confirmed.\nCheck in simulator: not confirmed.\nWhy: A failed payment must not be counted as a sale.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1tJuOwfbw-QCews6r6YS7DyDeJSIcPkOy/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"fad85ff0-85d8-4107-80b8-ed12e0a94179","module_id":"5ed0a17f-83ab-4746-b1d6-8ab738d6f9eb","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:22.167423+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:22.167423+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"Collect cross-module evidence for the report","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Supermarket - fictional grocery retail BA case. MODULE FILES: Read the file linked in this lesson. Keep the original source file unchanged.\nDO: Trace the correct records from M1 through M6 and the source pack; reject unsupported causal or approval claims.\n CHECK: Record source-supported evidence; BA recommendations are not system-change approvals.","duration":"35","lesson_id":"fb707ee3-b8c6-4c40-9d2a-2b27a266aee0","module_id":"61953943-322d-4034-ad05-89c9b5a237af","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:29.274549+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:50:29.274549+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2},{"title":"Explore the Final Challenge (optional presentation)","content":"The runner has a broken coin sequence. Look for the mistake, then plan a new pattern for another player. The final slides explain how to review and save your Pattern Passport.","duration":null,"lesson_id":"fb7b52fb-7bd4-4792-8a32-caaa167684a9","module_id":"d761eb0b-f00c-4dd6-9f36-b7f2f65f8f65","created_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:48.90121+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T09:47:48.90121+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Read the working-capital assignment","content":"WORKPLACE: Sri Lakshmi Foods - fictional finance workplace case. MODULE FILES: Open the linked guided deck and use the module source and learner workbook from the same Drive course folder.\nDO: Understand why overdue balances and slow inventory affect cash priorities; note the agreed 15-day customer credit term and 12-day stock target.\n CHECK: Save the source-supported output and carry unresolved items to the next task; management approvals are not implied.","duration":"20","lesson_id":"fbf4a2e2-72e1-45e5-a20c-88b1b0d4ef8f","module_id":"c02814cb-fc5f-4e0c-8756-451d7d0843a4","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:57.408634+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:57.408634+00:00","description":null,"order_index":1},{"title":"Empower: Marketing and Sales Analytics","content":"MODULE 4: Marketing and Sales Analytics\n6E STAGE: Empower\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nBUILD THE MARKETING & SALES POWER BI DASHBOARD\nLoad Mkt_Campaign and Sales_Lead; use Month / Period, Region and Channel / Lead Source dimensions.\nCreate Spend, Leads, Conversions, ROAS, Cost per Conversion, Closed Leads and Win Rate measures.\nAdd ROAS by Channel, Spend vs Conversions, Win Rate and Objection visuals.\nAdd Region and Period slicers.\n\nRESOURCE: M4_Marketing_and_Sales_Empower.pptx","duration":null,"lesson_id":"fc3318d9-efa4-4d32-8b0d-39d1b3cbef02","module_id":"42b2abe9-d25a-4686-8887-58a6810cdd28","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:28.52365+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:28.52365+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"Express: HR Analytics","content":"MODULE 3: HR Analytics\n6E STAGE: Express\nSOURCE SLIDE CONTENT:\nEXPECTED EXCEL DASHBOARD — HR\n\nRESOURCE: M3_HR_Express.pptx\n\nWORKSHEET TO COMPLETE: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M3_Express_Workforce_Recruitment_Risk_Diagnostic.xlsx\n\nCOMPANION WORKSHEET: MBA_Excel_PowerBI_M3_Express_Workforce_Recruitment_Risk_Diagnostic.xlsx\nWORKSHEET LINK: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1tS6GugNAWZ3iWcAsW5zG4qR8A2VTDuGk/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=116450298944087782964&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":null,"lesson_id":"fc6787a4-8c19-40df-bf9c-bf9ed8817b21","module_id":"8759a2fe-d783-4917-9716-d5383a2387ac","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:24.047431+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:40:24.047431+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"S16 - Export local drafts","content":"WHAT: We are downloading a JSON backup of device-local drafts.\nDO: Export local draft entries as a JSON backup downloaded by the browser.\nRUN / RESULT / CHECK: The browser downloads grama_drafts_backup.json containing local draft records.\nIF IT FAILS: Check the Downloads folder and JSON structure rather than relying only on a button click.\nSOURCE: Linked Module 03 PowerPoint, task S16 (original V25 teaching content).\nEVIDENCE: Grama_Learner_Evidence.xlsx > S01_S43_EXECUTION, row S16.","duration":"50","lesson_id":"fc9c660a-625b-4df9-aea0-c0bfc8543a7c","module_id":"725cf25c-1179-43c1-92b8-a16610df08b7","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:42.031583+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:48:42.031583+00:00","description":null,"order_index":4},{"title":"CA-002 Step 6 - Reconcile and hand over","content":"Independent challenge CA-002: NEON NIGHT DUOS, a new fictional 2v2 PIXEL RUSH gaming event.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nStarting evidence: 4 paid teams, 8 open places, ₹2,400 maximum ad spend, ₹600 fee per duo. Event date: 30 November 2026.\nOpen: CA-002 in the same offline simulator. Work without copying the CLUTCH ARENA worked answers.\n1. Match events to captured payments\n2. Count each genuine payment once\n3. Report actual results, not hoped-for results\nCheck: submit the result in the simulator; correct mistakes using the source records.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nEvidence: save the new-case results and report actual outcomes even if the target is missed.\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1CSnOPP3lw9hO3pH_k7PoG00toEfdGWDv/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"60","lesson_id":"fdb9ddfa-8321-4e16-aabc-15fe71cf2665","module_id":"0a68386e-3c99-4b9d-807f-26b8f5103ed8","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:49.744171+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:49.744171+00:00","description":null,"order_index":6},{"title":"T35 - Record simulated approval and launch","content":"Work task T35: Record simulated approval and launch.\nPRACTICE FILE - INTERACTIVE SIMULATOR: Use the linked resource in this lesson. Download the HTML file from Google Drive, then open it in Chrome or Edge; the Drive preview does not run the simulator. Keep the same file and browser for all modules.\nOpen: Ads Manager (practice) in the shared offline simulator.\n1. Check that the pre-launch report says PASS.\n2. Press Request manager approval (training).\n3. Press Simulate publish. Real work still needs human approval.\nCompleted example: Manager approval: Training simulation only; Real spend: ₹0; Delivery: In review.\nCheck in simulator: In review.\nWhy: A training button cannot grant real authority to spend a company budget.\nSimulator file: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gI5LWjKJZAE-__OzQo1vqFr1s6oHmOgu/view?usp=drivesdk\nMODULE SLIDES (PowerPoint): https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1izzDMQe1LDWcTfFFemfkzLiNafREVXsf/edit?usp=drivesdk&ouid=117748485795287437293&rtpof=true&sd=true","duration":"20","lesson_id":"fdec9dab-b62e-4ee7-8f3b-42800e1d1053","module_id":"9d37547e-5aca-4397-a704-05c09a59cb3a","created_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:38.073915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-06T08:49:38.073915+00:00","description":null,"order_index":2}]'::jsonb) r
WHERE r.module_id IN (SELECT module_id FROM public.course_modules WHERE course_id IN (SELECT id FROM lms_demo_missing_courses))
